/-!
# Finite pluriform representations for nef log curves

Let `C` be a smooth connected proper curve of genus `g` over an algebraically closed field `k` of
characteristic zero, `K` a canonical divisor and `B` a `ℚ`-divisor with `0 ≤ B ≤ 1` and
`deg (K + B) ≥ 0`. This file proves
`MMP.Fourfold.finite_range_pluriformPullback_and_isRelativelySemiample_of_curve`: the crepant
birational self-maps of `(C, B)` act on every `H⁰(C, m(K + B))` through a finite set of maps, and
`K + B` is semiample.

**Finiteness.** A crepant birational self-map is a `k`-automorphism `σ` of the function field.
Every such automorphism permutes the points of `C`: the valuation `ord_P ∘ σ` has a center `Q` by
the valuative criterion of properness, and `ord_P (σ f) = ord_Q f`. Crepancy says that the
coefficients of `B` are preserved, because the log discrepancy of `P` is `1 - coeff_P B`. Fix a
basis `ω` of the rational differentials and the derivation `D` with `d f = D(f) ω`. Then
`σ^* ω = h_σ ω`, `D (σ g) = h_σ σ (D g)`, and on `H⁰(C, m(K + B)) = L(m(div ω + B)) ω^{⊗m}` the
pull-back is `f ω^{⊗m} ↦ σ(f) h_σ^m ω^{⊗m}`.

The finiteness of this action is proved on the function field. A nontrivial automorphism fixes
at most `2g + 2` points, since `f - σ f` has poles of total order at most `2g + 2` for `f` with a
single pole of order at most `g + 1`. For `g ≥ 1` and `deg (K + B) > 0`, the Wronskian of a basis
of a linear system `L(D)` of degree at least `3g + 2` invariant under the group defines weights
`w_P = ∑ (a_i(P) - i)` (the `a_i(P)` the orders at `P`). Their sum is
`r deg D + r (r - 1)(g - 1)`, each weight is at most `r (deg D - r + 1)`, so more than `2g + 2`
points carry positive weight. That finite set is permuted, and the group embeds in its
permutations. For `g = 0` the support of `B` has at least three points unless `B = P₁ + P₂`; in
that case `D u / u` for `div u = P₁ - P₂` gives `σ^*` acting by `±1`. For `g = 1` and `B = 0` the
scalar `σ^*` on the one-dimensional `H⁰(C, mK)` has finite order. The stabilizer of a point is
finite, and any point is moved back to it by the involution of the quadratic extension
`k(C) / k(x)`, `x ∈ L(O + O')`.

**Semiampleness.** Choose `N > 0` with `N B` integral and put `D = N (K + B)`. If `deg D > 0`, then
`𝒪_C((2g + 1) D)` is generated by its global sections [Stacks, Tag 0E3C]. If `deg D = 0`, then
`g ≤ 1`, and in genus zero every invertible sheaf of degree zero is trivial, while in genus one
`B = 0` and `𝒪_C(K)` is trivial [Stacks, Tag 0B40].

## Main results

* `MMP.Fourfold.finite_range_pluriformPullback_and_isRelativelySemiample_of_curve`.

## Implementation notes

The finiteness is proved through an abstract function field of a curve: a field `K` over `k` with
a set of points carrying orders of vanishing, residues in `k`, uniformizers, principal divisors of
degree zero, the Riemann–Roch inequality `h⁰(D) ≥ deg D + 1 - g`, and a derivation dual to a
rational differential of degree `2g - 2`. The function field of `C` is shown to be one. The
genus-two-and-higher case uses the Weierstrass-type weights of a pluricanonical system and the
fixed-point bound (as in the classical proof that the automorphism group of a curve of genus at
least two is finite) instead of the algebraic group of projective transformations preserving the
tricanonical curve.

The sheaf `𝒪_C(E)` of a Cartier divisor is identified with the divisorial sheaf of its Weil
divisor by `MMP.Intersection.IsWeilDivisorOfCartier.nonempty_sheaf_iso_divisorialSheaf`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0E3C](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0E3C)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B40](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B40)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0C1E](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C1E)
-/

universe u

namespace MMP.Fourfold

namespace CurveAlg

open Module

/-- Abstract data of the function field of a smooth proper curve over `k`. -/
private structure CurveFF (k K Pt : Type*) [Field k] [Field K] [Algebra k K] where
  ord : Pt → K → ℤ
  ord_zero : ∀ P, ord P 0 = 0
  ord_mul : ∀ P (f g : K), f ≠ 0 → g ≠ 0 → ord P (f * g) = ord P f + ord P g
  ord_add : ∀ P (f g : K), f + g ≠ 0 → min (ord P f) (ord P g) ≤ ord P (f + g)
  ord_algebraMap : ∀ P (c : k), c ≠ 0 → ord P (algebraMap k K c) = 0
  residue : ∀ P (f : K), 0 ≤ ord P f →
    ∃ c : k, f = algebraMap k K c ∨ 1 ≤ ord P (f - algebraMap k K c)
  exists_uniformizer : ∀ P, ∃ t : K, ord P t = 1

variable {k K Pt : Type*} [Field k] [Field K] [Algebra k K] (C : CurveFF k K Pt)

namespace CurveFF

private theorem ord_one (P : Pt) : C.ord P 1 = 0 := by
  simpa using C.ord_algebraMap P 1 one_ne_zero

private theorem ord_neg (P : Pt) (f : K) : C.ord P (-f) = C.ord P f := by
  by_cases hf : f = 0
  · simp [hf]
  have h1 : C.ord P (-1) = 0 := by simpa using C.ord_algebraMap P (-1) (by simp)
  rw [show -f = -1 * f by ring, C.ord_mul P _ _ (by simp) hf, h1, zero_add]

private theorem ord_smul (P : Pt) {c : k} (hc : c ≠ 0) (f : K) : C.ord P (c • f) = C.ord P f := by
  by_cases hf : f = 0
  · simp [hf]
  rw [Algebra.smul_def, C.ord_mul P _ _ (by simpa using hc) hf, C.ord_algebraMap P c hc,
    zero_add]

private theorem ord_inv (P : Pt) {f : K} (hf : f ≠ 0) : C.ord P f⁻¹ = - C.ord P f := by
  have := C.ord_mul P f f⁻¹ hf (inv_ne_zero hf)
  rw [mul_inv_cancel₀ hf, C.ord_one] at this
  omega

private theorem ord_div (P : Pt) {f g : K} (hf : f ≠ 0) (hg : g ≠ 0) :
    C.ord P (f / g) = C.ord P f - C.ord P g := by
  rw [div_eq_mul_inv, C.ord_mul P _ _ hf (inv_ne_zero hg), C.ord_inv P hg]; ring

private theorem ord_pow (P : Pt) {f : K} (hf : f ≠ 0) (n : ℕ) :
    C.ord P (f ^ n) = n * C.ord P f := by
  induction n with
  | zero => simp [C.ord_one]
  | succ n ih => rw [pow_succ, C.ord_mul P _ _ (pow_ne_zero _ hf) hf, ih]; push_cast; ring

private theorem ord_zpow (P : Pt) {f : K} (hf : f ≠ 0) (n : ℤ) :
    C.ord P (f ^ n) = n * C.ord P f := by
  rcases n with n | n
  · simp [C.ord_pow P hf]
  · rw [zpow_negSucc, C.ord_inv P (pow_ne_zero _ hf), C.ord_pow P hf, Int.negSucc_eq]
    push_cast; ring

/-- Ultrametric inequality, including the degenerate cases. -/
private theorem le_ord_add (P : Pt) {n : ℤ} {f g : K} (hf : f = 0 ∨ n ≤ C.ord P f)
    (hg : g = 0 ∨ n ≤ C.ord P g) : f + g = 0 ∨ n ≤ C.ord P (f + g) := by
  by_cases hfg : f + g = 0
  · exact Or.inl hfg
  right
  rcases hf with rfl | hf
  · rcases hg with rfl | hg
    · simp at hfg
    · simpa using hg
  rcases hg with rfl | hg
  · simpa using hf
  exact (le_min hf hg).trans (C.ord_add P f g hfg)

private theorem ord_add_eq_of_lt (P : Pt) {f g : K} (hf : f ≠ 0) (hg : g ≠ 0)
    (h : C.ord P f < C.ord P g) : C.ord P (f + g) = C.ord P f := by
  have hfg : f + g ≠ 0 := by
    intro h0
    have : g = -f := by linear_combination h0
    rw [this, C.ord_neg] at h
    exact lt_irrefl _ h
  have h1 := C.ord_add P f g hfg
  rw [min_eq_left h.le] at h1
  have h2 := C.ord_add P (f + g) (-g) (by simpa using hf)
  rw [add_neg_cancel_right, C.ord_neg] at h2
  by_contra hne
  have : C.ord P f < C.ord P (f + g) := lt_of_le_of_ne h1 (Ne.symm hne)
  have := lt_min this h
  omega

/-- Subtracting a constant does not change the order at a pole. -/
private theorem ord_sub_algebraMap_of_neg (P : Pt) {f : K} (hf : f ≠ 0) (h : C.ord P f < 0)
    (c : k) : C.ord P (f - algebraMap k K c) = C.ord P f := by
  by_cases hc : c = 0
  · simp [hc]
  rw [sub_eq_add_neg, C.ord_add_eq_of_lt P hf (by simpa using hc)
    (by rw [C.ord_neg, C.ord_algebraMap P c hc]; exact h)]

/-- Subtracting a constant keeps a function without pole at `P` without pole at `P`. -/
private theorem ord_sub_algebraMap_nonneg (P : Pt) {f : K} (hf : 0 ≤ C.ord P f) {c : k}
    (h : f - algebraMap k K c ≠ 0) : 0 ≤ C.ord P (f - algebraMap k K c) := by
  rw [sub_eq_add_neg] at h ⊢
  refine (C.le_ord_add P (Or.inr hf) ?_).resolve_left h
  by_cases hc : c = 0
  · left; simp [hc]
  · right; rw [C.ord_neg, C.ord_algebraMap P c hc]

/-- The residue at `P` is unique. -/
private theorem residue_unique (P : Pt) {f : K} {c c' : k}
    (h : f = algebraMap k K c ∨ 1 ≤ C.ord P (f - algebraMap k K c))
    (h' : f = algebraMap k K c' ∨ 1 ≤ C.ord P (f - algebraMap k K c')) : c = c' := by
  by_contra hne
  have hd : algebraMap k K c' - algebraMap k K c = algebraMap k K (c' - c) := by simp
  have hne' : c' - c ≠ 0 := sub_ne_zero.mpr (Ne.symm hne)
  have key : (f - algebraMap k K c) + -(f - algebraMap k K c') = algebraMap k K (c' - c) := by
    rw [← hd]; ring
  have h1 : (f - algebraMap k K c) = 0 ∨ 1 ≤ C.ord P (f - algebraMap k K c) := by
    rcases h with h | h
    · left; rw [h, sub_self]
    · right; exact h
  have h2 : -(f - algebraMap k K c') = 0 ∨ 1 ≤ C.ord P (-(f - algebraMap k K c')) := by
    rcases h' with h' | h'
    · left; rw [h', sub_self, neg_zero]
    · right; rwa [C.ord_neg]
  rcases C.le_ord_add P h1 h2 with h3 | h3
  · rw [key] at h3
    exact hne' ((map_eq_zero_iff _ (algebraMap k K).injective).mp h3)
  · rw [key, C.ord_algebraMap P _ hne'] at h3
    omega

/-- The set of orders at `P` of the nonzero elements of a subspace. -/
private def ordSet (P : Pt) (L : Submodule k K) : Set ℤ := {a | ∃ f ∈ L, f ≠ 0 ∧ C.ord P f = a}

private theorem add_ne_zero_of_ord_ne (P : Pt) {f g : K} (hf : f ≠ 0)
    (h : C.ord P f ≠ C.ord P g) : f + g ≠ 0 := by
  intro h0
  have : g = -f := by linear_combination h0
  rw [this, C.ord_neg] at h
  exact h rfl

/-- A finite sum of nonzero functions with pairwise distinct orders is nonzero, of order the
least of the orders. -/
private theorem ord_sum_of_injOn {ι : Type*} (P : Pt) (s : Finset ι) (hs : s.Nonempty) (f : ι → K)
    (hf : ∀ i ∈ s, f i ≠ 0) (hinj : Set.InjOn (fun i => C.ord P (f i)) s) :
    ∃ i ∈ s, (∑ j ∈ s, f j) ≠ 0 ∧ C.ord P (∑ j ∈ s, f j) = C.ord P (f i) ∧
      ∀ j ∈ s, C.ord P (f i) ≤ C.ord P (f j) := by
  classical
  induction s using Finset.induction_on with
  | empty => exact absurd hs (by simp)
  | insert a s ha ih =>
    rcases s.eq_empty_or_nonempty with rfl | hsn
    · refine ⟨a, by simp, by simpa using hf a (by simp), by simp, by simp⟩
    obtain ⟨i, hi, hne, hord, hmin⟩ := ih hsn (fun j hj => hf j (Finset.mem_insert_of_mem hj))
      (hinj.mono (fun j hj => Finset.mem_insert_of_mem hj))
    have hai : C.ord P (f a) ≠ C.ord P (f i) := by
      intro h
      have := hinj (Finset.mem_insert_self a s) (Finset.mem_insert_of_mem hi) h
      exact ha (this ▸ hi)
    have hfa := hf a (Finset.mem_insert_self a s)
    rw [Finset.sum_insert ha]
    rcases lt_or_gt_of_ne hai with hlt | hgt
    · refine ⟨a, Finset.mem_insert_self a s, C.add_ne_zero_of_ord_ne P hfa (by omega),
        C.ord_add_eq_of_lt P hfa hne (hord ▸ hlt), ?_⟩
      intro j hj
      rcases Finset.mem_insert.mp hj with rfl | hj
      · exact le_rfl
      · exact hlt.le.trans (hmin j hj)
    · refine ⟨i, Finset.mem_insert_of_mem hi, ?_, ?_, ?_⟩
      · rw [add_comm]; exact C.add_ne_zero_of_ord_ne P hne (by omega)
      · rw [add_comm, C.ord_add_eq_of_lt P hne hfa (by omega), hord]
      · intro j hj
        rcases Finset.mem_insert.mp hj with rfl | hj
        · exact hgt.le
        · exact hmin j hj

private theorem le_ord_sum {ι : Type*} (P : Pt) (n : ℤ) (s : Finset ι) (g : ι → K)
    (hg : ∀ i ∈ s, g i = 0 ∨ n ≤ C.ord P (g i)) :
    ∑ i ∈ s, g i = 0 ∨ n ≤ C.ord P (∑ i ∈ s, g i) := by
  classical
  induction s using Finset.induction_on with
  | empty => simp
  | insert a s ha ih =>
    rw [Finset.sum_insert ha]
    exact C.le_ord_add P (hg a (Finset.mem_insert_self a s))
      (ih fun i hi => hg i (Finset.mem_insert_of_mem hi))

/-- The orders of the nonzero elements of a finite-dimensional subspace are bounded below. -/
private theorem exists_le_ord (P : Pt) (L : Submodule k K) [FiniteDimensional k L] :
    ∃ m : ℤ, ∀ f ∈ L, f ≠ 0 → m ≤ C.ord P f := by
  classical
  let b := Module.finBasis k L
  refine ⟨-∑ i, |C.ord P (b i : K)|, fun f hf hf0 => ?_⟩
  have hrepr : (f : K) = ∑ i, (b.repr ⟨f, hf⟩ i) • (b i : K) := by
    have h := congrArg Subtype.val (b.sum_repr ⟨f, hf⟩)
    simp only [Submodule.coe_sum, Submodule.coe_smul] at h
    exact h.symm
  have hbound : ∀ i, -∑ j, |C.ord P (b j : K)| ≤ C.ord P (b i : K) := by
    intro i
    have h1 : |C.ord P (b i : K)| ≤ ∑ j, |C.ord P (b j : K)| :=
      Finset.single_le_sum (f := fun j => |C.ord P (b j : K)|) (fun j _ => abs_nonneg _)
        (Finset.mem_univ i)
    have h2 := neg_abs_le (C.ord P (b i : K))
    linarith
  rcases C.le_ord_sum P (-∑ i, |C.ord P (b i : K)|) Finset.univ
      (fun i => (b.repr ⟨f, hf⟩ i) • (b i : K)) (fun i _ => by
      by_cases hc : b.repr ⟨f, hf⟩ i = 0
      · left; rw [hc, zero_smul]
      · right; rw [C.ord_smul P hc]; exact hbound i) with h | h
  · exact absurd (hrepr.trans h) hf0
  · rwa [← hrepr] at h

/-- The subspace of the elements of `L` of order greater than `m`. -/
private def ordGtSubmodule (P : Pt) (L : Submodule k K) (m : ℤ) : Submodule k K where
  carrier := {f | f ∈ L ∧ (f = 0 ∨ m + 1 ≤ C.ord P f)}
  zero_mem' := ⟨L.zero_mem, Or.inl rfl⟩
  add_mem' := fun hf hg => ⟨L.add_mem hf.1 hg.1, C.le_ord_add P hf.2 hg.2⟩
  smul_mem' := fun c f hf => by
    refine ⟨L.smul_mem c hf.1, ?_⟩
    by_cases hc : c = 0
    · left; rw [hc, zero_smul]
    rcases hf.2 with h | h
    · left; rw [h, smul_zero]
    · right; rwa [C.ord_smul P hc]

private theorem ordGtSubmodule_le (P : Pt) (L : Submodule k K) (m : ℤ) :
    C.ordGtSubmodule P L m ≤ L :=
  fun _ hf => hf.1

/-- **Orders and dimension.** The set of orders at `P` of the nonzero elements of a
finite-dimensional subspace `L` is finite, with `dim L` elements. -/
private theorem ordSet_finite_and_ncard (P : Pt) :
    ∀ (n : ℕ) (L : Submodule k K) [FiniteDimensional k L], finrank k L = n →
      (C.ordSet P L).Finite ∧ (C.ordSet P L).ncard = n := by
  intro n
  induction n with
  | zero =>
    intro L _ hL
    have : L = ⊥ := Submodule.finrank_eq_zero.mp hL
    subst this
    have : C.ordSet P ⊥ = ∅ := by
      ext a
      simp only [ordSet, Submodule.mem_bot, Set.mem_setOf_eq, Set.mem_empty_iff_false,
        iff_false, not_exists, not_and]
      exact fun f hf hf0 => absurd hf hf0
    rw [this]; exact ⟨Set.finite_empty, Set.ncard_empty _⟩
  | succ n ih =>
    intro L _ hL
    classical
    obtain ⟨m₀, hm₀⟩ := C.exists_le_ord P L
    have hne : (C.ordSet P L).Nonempty := by
      have : L ≠ ⊥ := by
        intro h; rw [h, finrank_bot] at hL; omega
      obtain ⟨f, hf, hf0⟩ := Submodule.exists_mem_ne_zero_of_ne_bot this
      exact ⟨_, f, hf, hf0, rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨m, ⟨g, hg, hg0, hgm⟩, hmin⟩ := Int.exists_least_of_bdd
      ⟨m₀, fun a ⟨f, hf, hf0, hfa⟩ => hfa ▸ hm₀ f hf hf0⟩ hne
    set L' := C.ordGtSubmodule P L m
    have hL'L : L' ≤ L := C.ordGtSubmodule_le P L m
    haveI : FiniteDimensional k L' := Submodule.finiteDimensional_of_le hL'L
    have hgL' : g ∉ L' := fun h => by
      rcases h.2 with h | h
      · exact hg0 h
      · omega
    have hdecomp : ∀ f ∈ L, ∃ c : k, f - c • g ∈ L' := by
      intro f hf
      by_cases hf0 : f = 0
      · exact ⟨0, by rw [hf0, zero_smul, sub_zero]; exact L'.zero_mem⟩
      have hfm : m ≤ C.ord P f := hmin _ ⟨f, hf, hf0, rfl⟩
      have hq : 0 ≤ C.ord P (f / g) := by rw [C.ord_div P hf0 hg0]; omega
      obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := C.residue P (f / g) hq
      refine ⟨c, L.sub_mem hf (L.smul_mem c hg), ?_⟩
      have hfc : f - c • g = g * (f / g - algebraMap k K c) := by
        rw [Algebra.smul_def]; field_simp
      rcases hc with hc | hc
      · left; rw [hfc, hc, sub_self, mul_zero]
      · by_cases h0 : f / g - algebraMap k K c = 0
        · left; rw [hfc, h0, mul_zero]
        · right; rw [hfc, C.ord_mul P _ _ hg0 h0, hgm]; omega
    have hsup : L' ⊔ Submodule.span k {g} = L := by
      apply le_antisymm (sup_le hL'L ((Submodule.span_singleton_le_iff_mem g L).mpr hg))
      intro f hf
      obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := hdecomp f hf
      have : f = (f - c • g) + c • g := by abel
      rw [this]
      exact Submodule.add_mem_sup hc (Submodule.smul_mem _ c (Submodule.mem_span_singleton_self g))
    have hinf : L' ⊓ Submodule.span k {g} = ⊥ := by
      rw [eq_bot_iff]
      intro f ⟨hf1, hf2⟩
      obtain ⟨c, rfl⟩ := Submodule.mem_span_singleton.mp hf2
      by_cases hc : c = 0
      · rw [hc, zero_smul]; exact Submodule.zero_mem _
      · exact absurd ((Submodule.smul_mem_iff L' hc).mp hf1) hgL'
    have hrank : finrank k L' = n := by
      have h := Submodule.finrank_sup_add_finrank_inf_eq L' (Submodule.span k {g})
      rw [hsup, hinf, finrank_bot, finrank_span_singleton hg0, add_zero, hL] at h
      omega
    obtain ⟨hfin, hcard⟩ := ih L' hrank
    have hset : C.ordSet P L = insert m (C.ordSet P L') := by
      ext a
      constructor
      · rintro ⟨f, hf, hf0, rfl⟩
        by_cases ha : C.ord P f = m
        · exact Or.inl ha
        · have hfm : m ≤ C.ord P f := hmin _ ⟨f, hf, hf0, rfl⟩
          exact Or.inr ⟨f, ⟨hf, Or.inr (by omega)⟩, hf0, rfl⟩
      · rintro (rfl | ⟨f, hf, hf0, rfl⟩)
        · exact ⟨g, hg, hg0, hgm⟩
        · exact ⟨f, hL'L hf, hf0, rfl⟩
    have hmnot : m ∉ C.ordSet P L' := by
      rintro ⟨f, hf, hf0, hfm⟩
      rcases hf.2 with h | h
      · exact hf0 h
      · omega
    rw [hset]
    exact ⟨hfin.insert m, by rw [Set.ncard_insert_of_notMem hmnot hfin, hcard]⟩

end CurveFF

/-- Global data of the function field of a smooth proper connected curve over `k`. -/
private structure ProperCurveFF (k K Pt : Type*) [Field k] [Field K] [Algebra k K]
    extends CurveFF k K Pt where
  nonempty : Nonempty Pt
  finite_support : ∀ f : K, f ≠ 0 → (Function.support fun P => ord P f).Finite
  deg_div : ∀ (f : K) (hf : f ≠ 0),
    (Finsupp.ofSupportFinite _ (finite_support f hf)).sum (fun _ a => a) = 0
  const : ∀ f : K, (∀ P, 0 ≤ ord P f) → ∃ c : k, f = algebraMap k K c

namespace ProperCurveFF

variable (C : ProperCurveFF k K Pt)

/-- The divisor of a nonzero function. -/
private noncomputable def div (f : K) (hf : f ≠ 0) : Pt →₀ ℤ :=
  Finsupp.ofSupportFinite _ (C.finite_support f hf)

/-- The divisor of a nonzero function `f` takes the value `ord P f` at each point `P`. -/
@[simp]
theorem div_apply (f : K) (hf : f ≠ 0) (P : Pt) : C.div f hf P = C.ord P f := rfl

/-- The degree of a divisor. -/
private def deg (D : Pt →₀ ℤ) : ℤ := D.sum fun _ a => a

private theorem deg_add (D E : Pt →₀ ℤ) : deg (D + E) = deg D + deg E := by
  unfold deg; exact Finsupp.sum_add_index' (fun _ => rfl) (fun _ _ _ => rfl)

private theorem deg_smul (n : ℤ) (D : Pt →₀ ℤ) : deg (n • D) = n * deg D := by
  unfold deg
  rw [Finsupp.sum_smul_index (fun _ => rfl), Finsupp.mul_sum]

private theorem deg_single (P : Pt) (n : ℤ) : deg (Finsupp.single P n) = n := by
  unfold deg; simp

private theorem deg_div_eq_zero (f : K) (hf : f ≠ 0) : deg (C.div f hf) = 0 := C.deg_div f hf

private theorem le_deg_of_nonneg {E : Pt →₀ ℤ} (hE : ∀ Q, 0 ≤ E Q) (P : Pt) : E P ≤ deg E := by
  classical
  unfold deg Finsupp.sum
  by_cases hP : P ∈ E.support
  · exact Finset.single_le_sum (f := ⇑E) (fun Q _ => hE Q) hP
  · rw [Finsupp.notMem_support_iff.mp hP]
    exact Finset.sum_nonneg fun Q _ => hE Q

/-- The space `L(D)` of the functions `f` with `div f + D ≥ 0`. -/
private def lin (D : Pt →₀ ℤ) : Submodule k K where
  carrier := {f | f = 0 ∨ ∀ P, 0 ≤ C.ord P f + D P}
  zero_mem' := Or.inl rfl
  add_mem' := fun {f g} hf hg => by
    by_cases hfg : f + g = 0
    · exact Or.inl hfg
    refine Or.inr fun P => ?_
    have h1 : f = 0 ∨ -D P ≤ C.ord P f := hf.imp_right fun h => by have := h P; omega
    have h2 : g = 0 ∨ -D P ≤ C.ord P g := hg.imp_right fun h => by have := h P; omega
    rcases C.le_ord_add P h1 h2 with h | h
    · exact absurd h hfg
    · omega
  smul_mem' := fun c f hf => by
    by_cases hc : c = 0
    · left; rw [hc, zero_smul]
    rcases hf with h | h
    · left; rw [h, smul_zero]
    · right; intro P; rw [C.ord_smul P hc]; exact h P

/-- For `f ∈ L(D)` nonzero, `ord_P f + D_P ≤ deg D`. -/
private theorem ord_add_le_deg {D : Pt →₀ ℤ} {f : K} (hf : f ∈ C.lin D) (hf0 : f ≠ 0) (P : Pt) :
    C.ord P f + D P ≤ deg D := by
  have hE : ∀ Q, 0 ≤ (C.div f hf0 + D) Q := fun Q => by
    rcases hf with h | h
    · exact absurd h hf0
    · simpa using h Q
  have := le_deg_of_nonneg hE P
  rwa [deg_add, C.deg_div_eq_zero, zero_add] at this

private theorem ordSet_subset_Icc {D : Pt →₀ ℤ} {L : Submodule k K} (h : L ≤ C.lin D) (P : Pt) :
    C.ordSet P L ⊆ ↑(Finset.Icc (-D P) (deg D - D P)) := by
  rintro a ⟨f, hf, hf0, rfl⟩
  have h1 := C.ord_add_le_deg (h hf) hf0 P
  have h2 : 0 ≤ C.ord P f + D P := by
    rcases h hf with h | h
    · exact absurd h hf0
    · exact h P
  simp only [Finset.coe_Icc, Set.mem_Icc]
  constructor <;> omega

private theorem finrank_le_of_le_lin {D : Pt →₀ ℤ} (L : Submodule k K) [FiniteDimensional k L]
    (h : L ≤ C.lin D) : (finrank k L : ℤ) ≤ max (deg D + 1) 0 := by
  obtain ⟨P⟩ := C.nonempty
  obtain ⟨hfin, hcard⟩ := C.ordSet_finite_and_ncard P _ L rfl
  have h1 := Set.ncard_le_ncard (C.ordSet_subset_Icc h P) (Finset.finite_toSet _)
  rw [hcard, Set.ncard_coe_finset, Int.card_Icc] at h1
  have : ((deg D - D P + 1 - -D P).toNat : ℤ) = max (deg D + 1) 0 := by
    rw [Int.toNat_eq_max]; congr 1; ring
  rw [← this]; exact_mod_cast h1

private theorem finiteDimensional_lin (D : Pt →₀ ℤ) : FiniteDimensional k (C.lin D) := by
  classical
  have hrank : Module.rank k (C.lin D) ≤ ((deg D + 1).toNat : ℕ) := by
    refine rank_le fun s hs => ?_
    let L : Submodule k K := Submodule.span k ((fun x : C.lin D => (x : K)) '' (s : Set _))
    have hL : L ≤ C.lin D := Submodule.span_le.mpr (by
      rintro _ ⟨x, -, rfl⟩; exact x.2)
    haveI : FiniteDimensional k L := FiniteDimensional.span_of_finite k
      ((Finset.finite_toSet s).image _)
    have h1 := C.finrank_le_of_le_lin L hL
    have hli : LinearIndependent k (fun x : (s : Set (C.lin D)) => ((x : C.lin D) : K)) :=
      (LinearIndependent.map' hs (C.lin D).subtype (Submodule.ker_subtype _))
    have h2 : finrank k L = s.card := by
      have := finrank_span_eq_card hli
      have hL' : L = Submodule.span k
          (Set.range fun x : (s : Set (C.lin D)) => ((x : C.lin D) : K)) := by
        simp only [L, ← Set.image_eq_range]
      rw [hL', this]; simp
    rw [h2] at h1
    omega
  exact Module.rank_lt_aleph0_iff.mp (hrank.trans_lt (Cardinal.natCast_lt_aleph0))

attribute [local instance] finiteDimensional_lin

private theorem finrank_lin_le (D : Pt →₀ ℤ) : (finrank k (C.lin D) : ℤ) ≤ max (deg D + 1) 0 :=
  C.finrank_le_of_le_lin _ le_rfl

/-- A subspace of dimension at least two contains a nonconstant function. -/
private theorem exists_mem_not_const {L : Submodule k K} [FiniteDimensional k L]
    (hL : 2 ≤ finrank k L) :
    ∃ f ∈ L, ∀ c : k, f ≠ algebraMap k K c := by
  by_contra h
  push Not at h
  have hle : L ≤ Submodule.span k {(1 : K)} := by
    intro f hf
    obtain ⟨c, rfl⟩ := h f hf
    rw [Algebra.algebraMap_eq_smul_one]
    exact Submodule.smul_mem _ c (Submodule.mem_span_singleton_self 1)
  have := Submodule.finrank_mono hle
  rw [finrank_span_singleton one_ne_zero] at this
  omega

end ProperCurveFF

attribute [local instance] ProperCurveFF.finiteDimensional_lin

/-- The function field of a smooth proper connected curve of genus `genus`, with the
Riemann–Roch inequality. -/
private structure CurveFFRR (k K Pt : Type*) [Field k] [Field K] [Algebra k K]
    extends ProperCurveFF k K Pt where
  genus : ℕ
  rr : ∀ D : Pt →₀ ℤ, ProperCurveFF.deg D + 1 - genus ≤ (finrank k (toProperCurveFF.lin D) : ℤ)

namespace CurveFFRR

variable (C : CurveFFRR k K Pt)

open ProperCurveFF

/-- Every point is the only pole of some function, of order at most `g + 1`. -/
private theorem exists_pole_only_at (P : Pt) :
    ∃ f : K, f ≠ 0 ∧ -(C.genus + 1 : ℤ) ≤ C.ord P f ∧ C.ord P f < 0 ∧
      ∀ Q, Q ≠ P → 0 ≤ C.ord Q f := by
  classical
  set D : Pt →₀ ℤ := Finsupp.single P ((C.genus : ℤ) + 1)
  have hrr := C.rr D
  rw [deg_single] at hrr
  obtain ⟨f, hf, hfc⟩ := exists_mem_not_const (L := C.lin D) (by omega)
  have hf0 : f ≠ 0 := fun h => hfc 0 (by rw [h, map_zero])
  rcases hf with h | h
  · exact absurd h hf0
  have hQ : ∀ Q, Q ≠ P → 0 ≤ C.ord Q f := fun Q hQ => by
    have := h Q; rwa [Finsupp.single_eq_of_ne hQ, add_zero] at this
  refine ⟨f, hf0, by have := h P; simp [D] at this; omega, ?_, hQ⟩
  by_contra hP
  push Not at hP
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := C.const f fun Q => by
    by_cases hQP : Q = P
    · rw [hQP]; exact hP
    · exact hQ Q hQP
  exact hfc c hc

/-- Functions separate points. -/
private theorem exists_ord_ne {Q Q' : Pt} (h : Q ≠ Q') : ∃ f : K, C.ord Q f ≠ C.ord Q' f := by
  obtain ⟨f, -, -, hf, hf'⟩ := C.exists_pole_only_at Q
  exact ⟨f, by have := hf' Q' (Ne.symm h); omega⟩

private theorem eq_of_ord_eq {Q Q' : Pt} (h : ∀ f : K, C.ord Q f = C.ord Q' f) : Q = Q' := by
  by_contra hne
  obtain ⟨f, hf⟩ := C.exists_ord_ne hne
  exact hf (h f)

/-- `π` is the permutation of points induced by the automorphism `σ` of the function field:
`ord_P (σ f) = ord_{π P} f`. -/
private def IsPointMap (σ : K ≃ₐ[k] K) (π : Pt → Pt) : Prop :=
  ∀ P (f : K), C.ord P (σ f) = C.ord (π P) f

private theorem IsPointMap.unique {σ : K ≃ₐ[k] K} {π π' : Pt → Pt} (h : C.IsPointMap σ π)
    (h' : C.IsPointMap σ π') : π = π' :=
  funext fun P => C.eq_of_ord_eq fun f => by rw [← h P f, ← h' P f]

private theorem isPointMap_one : C.IsPointMap 1 id := fun _ _ => rfl

private theorem IsPointMap.mul {σ τ : K ≃ₐ[k] K} {π ρ : Pt → Pt} (h : C.IsPointMap σ π)
    (h' : C.IsPointMap τ ρ) : C.IsPointMap (σ * τ) (ρ ∘ π) := fun P f => by
  change C.ord P (σ (τ f)) = _
  rw [h P, h' (π P)]
  rfl

private theorem IsPointMap.injective {σ : K ≃ₐ[k] K} {π : Pt → Pt} (h : C.IsPointMap σ π) :
    Function.Injective π := fun P Q hPQ => C.eq_of_ord_eq fun f => by
  rw [← σ.apply_symm_apply f, h P, h Q, hPQ]

private theorem IsPointMap.comp_inv {σ : K ≃ₐ[k] K} {π π' : Pt → Pt} (h : C.IsPointMap σ π)
    (h' : C.IsPointMap σ⁻¹ π') : π' ∘ π = id := by
  have := IsPointMap.mul C h h'
  rw [mul_inv_cancel] at this
  exact IsPointMap.unique C this C.isPointMap_one

private theorem IsPointMap.inv_comp {σ : K ≃ₐ[k] K} {π π' : Pt → Pt} (h : C.IsPointMap σ π)
    (h' : C.IsPointMap σ⁻¹ π') : π ∘ π' = id := by
  have := IsPointMap.mul C h' h
  rw [inv_mul_cancel] at this
  exact IsPointMap.unique C this C.isPointMap_one

/-- An automorphism fixing every point is the identity. -/
private theorem eq_one_of_isPointMap_id {σ : K ≃ₐ[k] K} (h : C.IsPointMap σ id) : σ = 1 := by
  have hscal : ∀ f : K, f ≠ 0 → ∃ c : k, σ f = algebraMap k K c * f := by
    intro f hf
    have hσf : σ f ≠ 0 := by simpa using hf
    obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := C.const (σ f / f) fun P => by
      rw [C.ord_div P hσf hf, h P f]; simp
    exact ⟨c, by rw [← hc]; field_simp⟩
  ext f
  by_cases hfc : ∃ c : k, f = algebraMap k K c
  · obtain ⟨c, rfl⟩ := hfc; exact σ.commutes c
  push Not at hfc
  have hf0 : f ≠ 0 := fun h => hfc 0 (by rw [h, map_zero])
  have hf1 : f - 1 ≠ 0 := fun h => hfc 1 (by rw [map_one]; linear_combination h)
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := hscal f hf0
  obtain ⟨c', hc'⟩ := hscal (f - 1) hf1
  have e : algebraMap k K c * f - 1 = algebraMap k K c' * (f - 1) := by
    rw [← hc, ← hc', map_sub, map_one]
  by_cases hcc : c = c'
  · subst hcc
    have : algebraMap k K c = 1 := by linear_combination e
    rw [hc, this, one_mul]; rfl
  · exfalso
    have hne : algebraMap k K (c - c') ≠ 0 := by
      rw [Ne, map_eq_zero_iff _ (algebraMap k K).injective]; exact sub_ne_zero.mpr hcc
    apply hfc ((1 - c') / (c - c'))
    rw [map_div₀, map_sub, map_sub, map_one]
    rw [map_sub] at hne
    field_simp
    linear_combination e

private theorem exists_ne_of_ne_one {σ : K ≃ₐ[k] K} {π : Pt → Pt} (h : C.IsPointMap σ π)
    (hσ : σ ≠ 1) :
    ∃ P, π P ≠ P := by
  by_contra hc
  push Not at hc
  have : π = id := funext hc
  exact hσ (C.eq_one_of_isPointMap_id (this ▸ h))

/-- Counting points of a set where an effective divisor is positive. -/
private theorem ncard_le_deg {E : Pt →₀ ℤ} (hE : ∀ Q, 0 ≤ E Q) {S : Set Pt}
    (hS : ∀ Q ∈ S, 1 ≤ E Q) :
    S.Finite ∧ (S.ncard : ℤ) ≤ deg E := by
  classical
  have hsub : S ⊆ ↑E.support := fun Q hQ => by
    have := hS Q hQ; simp only [Finset.mem_coe, Finsupp.mem_support_iff]; omega
  have hfin : S.Finite := (Finset.finite_toSet _).subset hsub
  refine ⟨hfin, ?_⟩
  have h1 : (S.ncard : ℤ) = ∑ Q ∈ hfin.toFinset, (1 : ℤ) := by
    simp [Set.ncard_eq_toFinset_card S hfin]
  rw [h1]
  calc ∑ Q ∈ hfin.toFinset, (1 : ℤ) ≤ ∑ Q ∈ hfin.toFinset, E Q :=
        Finset.sum_le_sum fun Q hQ => hS Q (by simpa using hQ)
    _ ≤ ∑ Q ∈ E.support, E Q := Finset.sum_le_sum_of_subset_of_nonneg
        (by intro Q hQ; exact hsub (by simpa using hQ)) (fun Q _ _ => hE Q)
    _ = deg E := rfl

/-- **Fixed points of an automorphism.** A nontrivial automorphism of the function field of a
curve of genus `g` which permutes the points fixes at most `2 g + 2` of them. -/
private theorem fixedPoints_finite_and_ncard_le {σ : K ≃ₐ[k] K} {π π' : Pt → Pt}
    (h : C.IsPointMap σ π)
    (h' : C.IsPointMap σ⁻¹ π') (hσ : σ ≠ 1) :
    {Q | π Q = Q}.Finite ∧ ({Q | π Q = Q}.ncard : ℤ) ≤ 2 * (C.genus + 1) := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨P, hP⟩ := C.exists_ne_of_ne_one h hσ
  obtain ⟨f, hf0, hfg, hfP, hfQ⟩ := C.exists_pole_only_at P
  set Q₀ := π' P
  have hQ₀ : π Q₀ = P := congrFun (IsPointMap.inv_comp C h h') P
  have hσf : ∀ Q, C.ord Q (σ f) = C.ord (π Q) f := fun Q => h Q f
  set g : K := f - σ f
  have hg0 : g ≠ 0 := by
    intro hg
    have : f = σ f := sub_eq_zero.mp hg
    have h1 := hσf P
    rw [← this] at h1
    have := hfQ (π P) hP
    omega
  have hfl : ∀ Q, -(if P = Q then (C.genus + 1 : ℤ) else 0) ≤ C.ord Q f := fun Q => by
    by_cases hQ : P = Q
    · rw [if_pos hQ, ← hQ]; exact hfg
    · rw [if_neg hQ]; simpa using hfQ Q (Ne.symm hQ)
  have hgl : ∀ Q, min (C.ord Q f) (C.ord Q (σ f)) ≤ C.ord Q g := fun Q => by
    have := C.ord_add Q f (-(σ f)) (by simpa [g, sub_eq_add_neg] using hg0)
    rwa [C.ord_neg, ← sub_eq_add_neg] at this
  set E : Pt →₀ ℤ := C.div g hg0 + Finsupp.single P ((C.genus : ℤ) + 1) +
    Finsupp.single Q₀ ((C.genus : ℤ) + 1)
  have hEapp : ∀ Q, E Q = C.ord Q g + (if P = Q then (C.genus + 1 : ℤ) else 0) +
      (if Q₀ = Q then (C.genus + 1 : ℤ) else 0) := fun Q => by
    simp only [E, Finsupp.add_apply, div_apply, Finsupp.single_apply]
  have hE : ∀ Q, 0 ≤ E Q := fun Q => by
    rw [hEapp]
    have h1 := hfl Q
    have h2 : -(if Q₀ = Q then (C.genus + 1 : ℤ) else 0) ≤ C.ord Q (σ f) := by
      rw [hσf]
      have := hfl (π Q)
      by_cases hQ : Q₀ = Q
      · rw [if_pos hQ]
        rwa [if_pos (by rw [← hQ, hQ₀])] at this
      · rw [if_neg hQ]
        have hne : P ≠ π Q := fun hπ => hQ (by
          apply IsPointMap.injective C h; rw [← hπ, hQ₀])
        rwa [if_neg hne] at this
    have h3 := hgl Q
    have hP0 : (0 : ℤ) ≤ (if P = Q then (C.genus + 1 : ℤ) else 0) := by split_ifs <;> omega
    have hQ0 : (0 : ℤ) ≤ (if Q₀ = Q then (C.genus + 1 : ℤ) else 0) := by split_ifs <;> omega
    have := min_le_iff.mp h3
    omega
  have hfix : ∀ Q ∈ {Q | π Q = Q}, 1 ≤ E Q := by
    intro Q hQ
    simp only [Set.mem_setOf_eq] at hQ
    have hQP : Q ≠ P := fun hq => hP (hq ▸ hQ)
    have hQQ₀ : Q ≠ Q₀ := by
      intro hq
      have h1 : π Q = P := by rw [hq]; exact hQ₀
      exact hQP (hQ.symm.trans h1)
    rw [hEapp, if_neg (Ne.symm hQP), if_neg (Ne.symm hQQ₀), add_zero, add_zero]
    obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := C.residue Q f (hfQ Q hQP)
    have hc1 : f - algebraMap k K c = 0 ∨ 1 ≤ C.ord Q (f - algebraMap k K c) := by
      rcases hc with hc | hc
      · left; rw [hc, sub_self]
      · right; exact hc
    have hc2 : -(σ f - algebraMap k K c) = 0 ∨ 1 ≤ C.ord Q (-(σ f - algebraMap k K c)) := by
      have e : σ f - algebraMap k K c = σ (f - algebraMap k K c) := by
        rw [map_sub, AlgEquiv.commutes]
      rw [C.ord_neg, e, h Q, hQ, neg_eq_zero, map_eq_zero_iff _ σ.injective]
      exact hc1
    have e2 : (f - algebraMap k K c) + -(σ f - algebraMap k K c) = g := by simp [g]
    rcases C.le_ord_add Q hc1 hc2 with h4 | h4
    · rw [e2] at h4; exact absurd h4 hg0
    · rwa [e2] at h4
  obtain ⟨hfin, hcard⟩ := ncard_le_deg hE hfix
  refine ⟨hfin, hcard.trans (le_of_eq ?_)⟩
  simp only [E, deg_add, deg_div_eq_zero, deg_single]
  ring

/-- An automorphism fixing more than `2 g + 2` points is the identity. -/
private theorem eq_one_of_fixes {σ : K ≃ₐ[k] K} {π π' : Pt → Pt} (h : C.IsPointMap σ π)
    (h' : C.IsPointMap σ⁻¹ π') {S : Set Pt} (hS : S.Finite)
    (hcard : 2 * (C.genus + 1) < (S.ncard : ℤ))
    (hfix : ∀ Q ∈ S, π Q = Q) : σ = 1 := by
  by_contra hσ
  obtain ⟨hfin, hle⟩ := C.fixedPoints_finite_and_ncard_le h h' hσ
  have := Set.ncard_le_ncard (s := S) (t := {Q | π Q = Q}) (fun Q hQ => hfix Q hQ) hfin
  omega

/-- **Finiteness from an invariant set.** A set of automorphisms of the function field which
permute the points and preserve a finite set of more than `2 g + 2` points is finite. -/
private theorem finite_of_mapsTo (G : Set (K ≃ₐ[k] K)) (π π' : (K ≃ₐ[k] K) → Pt → Pt) {S : Set Pt}
    (hS : S.Finite) (hcard : 2 * (C.genus + 1) < (S.ncard : ℤ))
    (hG : ∀ σ ∈ G, C.IsPointMap σ (π σ) ∧ C.IsPointMap σ⁻¹ (π' σ) ∧ Set.MapsTo (π σ) S S) :
    G.Finite := by
  classical
  haveI : Finite S := hS.to_subtype
  let Φ : G → (S → S) := fun σ Q => ⟨π σ Q, (hG σ σ.2).2.2 Q.2⟩
  have hinj : Function.Injective Φ := by
    rintro ⟨σ, hσ⟩ ⟨τ, hτ⟩ hst
    obtain ⟨h1, h1', h1s⟩ := hG σ hσ
    obtain ⟨h2, h2', h2s⟩ := hG τ hτ
    have hρ : C.IsPointMap (σ⁻¹ * τ) (π τ ∘ π' σ) := IsPointMap.mul C h1' h2
    have hρ' : C.IsPointMap (σ⁻¹ * τ)⁻¹ (π σ ∘ π' τ) := by
      rw [mul_inv_rev, inv_inv]; exact IsPointMap.mul C h2' h1
    have hsurj : Set.SurjOn (π σ) S S :=
      (Set.Finite.injOn_iff_bijOn_of_mapsTo hS h1s).mp
        (IsPointMap.injective C h1).injOn |>.surjOn
    have hfix : ∀ Q ∈ S, (π τ ∘ π' σ) Q = Q := by
      intro Q hQ
      obtain ⟨Q', hQ', rfl⟩ := hsurj hQ
      have e1 : π' σ (π σ Q') = Q' := congrFun (IsPointMap.comp_inv C h1 h1') Q'
      have e2 : π τ Q' = π σ Q' := by
        have := congrArg Subtype.val (congrFun hst ⟨Q', hQ'⟩)
        exact this.symm
      simp only [Function.comp_apply, e1, e2]
    have := C.eq_one_of_fixes hρ hρ' hS hcard hfix
    have : τ = σ := by
      have h := congrArg (σ * ·) this
      simpa [mul_inv_cancel_left] using h
    exact Subtype.ext this.symm
  exact Set.finite_coe_iff.mp (Finite.of_injective Φ hinj)

end CurveFFRR

namespace CurveFF

/-- The local ring `𝒪_P` of the functions with no pole at `P`. -/
private def valRing (P : Pt) : Subring K where
  carrier := {x | x = 0 ∨ 0 ≤ C.ord P x}
  zero_mem' := Or.inl rfl
  one_mem' := Or.inr (by rw [C.ord_one])
  add_mem' := fun hx hy => C.le_ord_add P hx hy
  neg_mem' := fun {x} hx => by
    rcases hx with h | h
    · left; rw [h, neg_zero]
    · right; rwa [C.ord_neg]
  mul_mem' := fun {x y} hx hy => by
    by_cases hx0 : x = 0
    · left; rw [hx0, zero_mul]
    by_cases hy0 : y = 0
    · left; rw [hy0, mul_zero]
    right
    rw [C.ord_mul P x y hx0 hy0]
    rcases hx with h | h
    · exact absurd h hx0
    rcases hy with h' | h'
    · exact absurd h' hy0
    omega

private theorem algebraMap_mem_valRing (P : Pt) (c : k) : algebraMap k K c ∈ C.valRing P := by
  by_cases hc : c = 0
  · left; rw [hc, map_zero]
  · right; rw [C.ord_algebraMap P c hc]

/-- `c` is the residue of `x` at `P`. -/
private def IsRes (P : Pt) (x : K) (c : k) : Prop :=
  x - algebraMap k K c = 0 ∨ 1 ≤ C.ord P (x - algebraMap k K c)

private theorem isRes_unique {P : Pt} {x : K} {c c' : k} (h : C.IsRes P x c) (h' : C.IsRes P x c') :
    c = c' := by
  refine C.residue_unique P (f := x) ?_ ?_
  · rcases h with h | h
    · left; linear_combination h
    · right; exact h
  · rcases h' with h | h
    · left; linear_combination h
    · right; exact h

private theorem exists_isRes {P : Pt} {x : K} (hx : x ∈ C.valRing P) : ∃ c, C.IsRes P x c := by
  rcases hx with h | h
  · exact ⟨0, Or.inl (by rw [h, map_zero, sub_zero])⟩
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := C.residue P x h
  refine ⟨c, ?_⟩
  rcases hc with hc | hc
  · left; rw [hc, sub_self]
  · right; exact hc

private theorem IsRes.add {P : Pt} {x y : K} {c d : k} (hx : C.IsRes P x c) (hy : C.IsRes P y d) :
    C.IsRes P (x + y) (c + d) := by
  have e : x + y - algebraMap k K (c + d) = (x - algebraMap k K c) + (y - algebraMap k K d) := by
    rw [map_add]; ring
  unfold IsRes; rw [e]; exact C.le_ord_add P hx hy

private theorem IsRes.mul {P : Pt} {x y : K} {c d : k} (hx : C.IsRes P x c) (hy : C.IsRes P y d)
    (hyO : y ∈ C.valRing P) : C.IsRes P (x * y) (c * d) := by
  have e : x * y - algebraMap k K (c * d) =
      (x - algebraMap k K c) * y + algebraMap k K c * (y - algebraMap k K d) := by
    rw [map_mul]; ring
  unfold IsRes; rw [e]
  refine C.le_ord_add P ?_ ?_
  · rcases hx with h | h
    · left; rw [h, zero_mul]
    by_cases hy0 : y = 0
    · left; rw [hy0, mul_zero]
    rcases hyO with h' | h'
    · exact absurd h' hy0
    by_cases hx0 : x - algebraMap k K c = 0
    · left; rw [hx0, zero_mul]
    right; rw [C.ord_mul P _ _ hx0 hy0]; omega
  · by_cases hc : c = 0
    · left; rw [hc, map_zero, zero_mul]
    rcases hy with h | h
    · left; rw [h, mul_zero]
    by_cases hy0 : y - algebraMap k K d = 0
    · left; rw [hy0, mul_zero]
    right; rw [C.ord_mul P _ _ (by simpa using hc) hy0, C.ord_algebraMap P c hc, zero_add]
    exact h

private theorem isRes_algebraMap (P : Pt) (c : k) : C.IsRes P (algebraMap k K c) c :=
  Or.inl (sub_self _)

/-- The residue map `𝒪_P → k`. -/
private noncomputable def res (P : Pt) : C.valRing P →+* k where
  toFun x := (C.exists_isRes x.2).choose
  map_one' := C.isRes_unique (C.exists_isRes (C.valRing P).one_mem).choose_spec
    (by simpa using C.isRes_algebraMap P 1)
  map_mul' x y := C.isRes_unique (C.exists_isRes (x * y).2).choose_spec
    (IsRes.mul C (C.exists_isRes x.2).choose_spec (C.exists_isRes y.2).choose_spec y.2)
  map_zero' := C.isRes_unique (C.exists_isRes (C.valRing P).zero_mem).choose_spec
    (by simpa using C.isRes_algebraMap P 0)
  map_add' x y := C.isRes_unique (C.exists_isRes (x + y).2).choose_spec
    (IsRes.add C (C.exists_isRes x.2).choose_spec (C.exists_isRes y.2).choose_spec)

private theorem isRes_res (P : Pt) (x : C.valRing P) : C.IsRes P x (C.res P x) :=
  (C.exists_isRes x.2).choose_spec

private theorem res_eq_of_isRes {P : Pt} {x : C.valRing P} {c : k} (h : C.IsRes P x c) :
    C.res P x = c := C.isRes_unique (C.isRes_res P x) h

private theorem res_eq_zero_iff {P : Pt} (x : C.valRing P) :
    C.res P x = 0 ↔ (x : K) = 0 ∨ 1 ≤ C.ord P x := by
  constructor
  · intro h
    have := C.isRes_res P x
    rw [h] at this
    simpa [IsRes] using this
  · intro h
    apply C.res_eq_of_isRes
    simpa [IsRes] using h

/-- An element of `𝒪_P` with nonzero residue has order zero. -/
private theorem ord_eq_zero_of_res_ne_zero {P : Pt} (x : C.valRing P) (h : C.res P x ≠ 0) :
    C.ord P x = 0 := by
  have h1 : (x : K) ≠ 0 := fun h0 => h ((C.res_eq_zero_iff x).mpr (Or.inl h0))
  rcases x.2 with h2 | h2
  · exact absurd h2 h1
  · have : ¬ 1 ≤ C.ord P x := fun h3 => h ((C.res_eq_zero_iff x).mpr (Or.inr h3))
    omega

private theorem mem_valRing_of_isRes {P : Pt} {x : K} {c : k} (h : C.IsRes P x c) :
    x ∈ C.valRing P := by
  have : x = (x - algebraMap k K c) + algebraMap k K c := by ring
  rw [this]
  refine (C.valRing P).add_mem ?_ (C.algebraMap_mem_valRing P c)
  rcases h with h | h
  · left; exact h
  · right; omega

private theorem ne_zero_of_ord_eq_one {P : Pt} {t : K} (ht : C.ord P t = 1) : t ≠ 0 := by
  rintro rfl; rw [C.ord_zero] at ht; exact zero_ne_one ht

end CurveFF

private theorem Derivation.leibniz_zpow' {k K : Type*} [Field k] [Field K] [Algebra k K]
    (D : Derivation k K K) (x : K) (n : ℤ) :
    D (x ^ n) = (n : K) * x ^ (n - 1) * D x := by
  rw [Derivation.leibniz_zpow, smul_eq_mul, zsmul_eq_mul, mul_assoc]

namespace CurveFF

variable (D : Derivation k K K)

/-- For `u ∈ 𝒪_P`, `t D u / D t` lies in the maximal ideal. -/
private theorem isRes_mul_derivation_div {P : Pt} {t : K} (ht : C.ord P t = 1) (hD : D t ≠ 0)
    (hDO : ∀ u ∈ C.valRing P, D u = 0 ∨ C.ord P (D t) ≤ C.ord P (D u)) {u : K}
    (hu : u ∈ C.valRing P) : C.IsRes P (t * D u / D t) 0 := by
  unfold IsRes
  rw [map_zero, sub_zero]
  rcases hDO u hu with h | h
  · left; rw [h, mul_zero, zero_div]
  · by_cases h0 : t * D u / D t = 0
    · left; exact h0
    right
    have ht0 := C.ne_zero_of_ord_eq_one ht
    have hDu : D u ≠ 0 := fun h' => h0 (by rw [h', mul_zero, zero_div])
    rw [C.ord_div P (mul_ne_zero ht0 hDu) hD, C.ord_mul P _ _ ht0 hDu, ht]
    omega

/-- The residue of `t D(D t) / (D t)²` is the order of `D t`. -/
private theorem isRes_mul_derivation_div_sq {P : Pt} {t : K} (ht : C.ord P t = 1) (hD : D t ≠ 0)
    (hDO : ∀ u ∈ C.valRing P, D u = 0 ∨ C.ord P (D t) ≤ C.ord P (D u)) :
    C.IsRes P (t * D (D t) / (D t) ^ 2) (C.ord P (D t) : k) := by
  set h := D t
  set e := C.ord P h
  have ht0 := C.ne_zero_of_ord_eq_one ht
  set v := h / t ^ e
  have hte : t ^ e ≠ 0 := zpow_ne_zero _ ht0
  have hv0 : v ≠ 0 := div_ne_zero hD hte
  have hvord : C.ord P v = 0 := by
    rw [C.ord_div P hD hte, C.ord_zpow P ht0, ht]; ring
  have hvO : v ∈ C.valRing P := Or.inr (by rw [hvord])
  have hhv : h = t ^ e * v := by simp only [v]; field_simp
  have hDh : D h = (e : K) * t ^ (e - 1) * D t * v + t ^ e * D v := by
    conv_lhs => rw [hhv]
    rw [Derivation.leibniz, Derivation.leibniz_zpow' D t, smul_eq_mul, smul_eq_mul]; ring
  set s := t ^ (e - 1)
  have hts : t ^ e = t * s := by simp only [s]; rw [← zpow_one_add₀ ht0]; ring_nf
  have h2 : h = t * s * v := by rw [hhv, hts]
  have hs0 : s ≠ 0 := zpow_ne_zero _ ht0
  have key : t * D h / h ^ 2 - algebraMap k K (e : k) = t * D v / (D t) / v := by
    rw [map_intCast, hDh, hts]
    change t * (↑e * s * h * v + t * s * D v) / h ^ 2 - ↑e = t * D v / h / v
    rw [h2]
    field_simp
    ring
  unfold IsRes
  rw [key]
  have h1 := C.isRes_mul_derivation_div D ht hD hDO hvO
  unfold IsRes at h1
  rw [map_zero, sub_zero] at h1
  rcases h1 with h1 | h1
  · left; rw [h1, zero_div]
  · by_cases h0 : t * D v / D t / v = 0
    · left; exact h0
    right
    have hne : t * D v / D t ≠ 0 := fun h' => h0 (by rw [h', zero_div])
    rw [C.ord_div P hne hv0, hvord, sub_zero]
    exact h1

private theorem Derivation.leibniz_pow' {k K : Type*} [Field k] [Field K] [Algebra k K]
    (D : Derivation k K K) {x : K} (hx : x ≠ 0) (j : ℕ) :
    D (x ^ j) = (j : K) * x ^ j / x * D x := by
  rw [Derivation.leibniz_pow, nsmul_eq_mul, smul_eq_mul]
  rcases j with _ | j
  · simp
  · rw [pow_succ]; field_simp; push_cast; ring

/-- **Iterated derivatives at a point.** For `t` a uniformizer at `P`, `h = D t`, `e = ord_P h`
and `u ∈ 𝒪_P` of residue `c`, `D^j (t^a u) = t^(a - j) h^j w` with `w ∈ 𝒪_P` of residue
`∏_{i < j} (a - i + i e) · c`. -/
private theorem iterate_derivation_zpow_mul {P : Pt} {t : K} (ht : C.ord P t = 1) (hD : D t ≠ 0)
    (hDO : ∀ u ∈ C.valRing P, D u = 0 ∨ C.ord P (D t) ≤ C.ord P (D u)) (a : ℤ) {u : K} {c : k}
    (hu : C.IsRes P u c) (j : ℕ) :
    ∃ w : K, C.IsRes P w ((∏ i ∈ Finset.range j, ((a : k) - i + i * C.ord P (D t))) * c) ∧
      (⇑D)^[j] (t ^ a * u) = t ^ (a - j) * (D t) ^ j * w := by
  have ht0 := C.ne_zero_of_ord_eq_one ht
  induction j with
  | zero => exact ⟨u, by simpa using hu, by simp⟩
  | succ j ih =>
    obtain ⟨w, hw, hwe⟩ := ih
    have hwO := C.mem_valRing_of_isRes hw
    set h := D t
    set e := C.ord P h
    set q := t * D h / h ^ 2
    have hq := C.isRes_mul_derivation_div_sq D ht hD hDO
    have hqO := C.mem_valRing_of_isRes hq
    set r := (∏ i ∈ Finset.range j, ((a : k) - i + i * e)) * c
    refine ⟨algebraMap k K ((a : k) - j) * w + algebraMap k K (j : k) * (q * w) + t * D w / h,
      ?_, ?_⟩
    · have h1 := IsRes.mul C (C.isRes_algebraMap P ((a : k) - j)) hw hwO
      have h2 := IsRes.mul C (C.isRes_algebraMap P (j : k)) (IsRes.mul C hq hw hwO)
        ((C.valRing P).mul_mem hqO hwO)
      have h3 := C.isRes_mul_derivation_div D ht hD hDO hwO
      have h4 := IsRes.add C (IsRes.add C h1 h2) h3
      have e4 : ((a : k) - j) * r + j * ((e : k) * r) + 0 =
          (∏ i ∈ Finset.range (j + 1), ((a : k) - i + i * e)) * c := by
        rw [Finset.prod_range_succ]; simp only [r]; ring
      rwa [e4] at h4
    · rw [Function.iterate_succ_apply', hwe]
      set T := t ^ (a - ((j + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ))
      have hT : t ^ (a - (j : ℤ)) = T * t := by
        simp only [T]; rw [← zpow_add_one₀ ht0]; congr 1; push_cast; ring
      have hDT : D (t ^ (a - (j : ℤ))) = ((a : K) - j) * T * h := by
        rw [Derivation.leibniz_zpow' D t]
        simp only [T]; push_cast; congr 2; ring_nf
      have hDh : D (h ^ j) = (j : K) * h ^ j / h * D h :=
        Derivation.leibniz_pow' D hD j
      rw [Derivation.leibniz, Derivation.leibniz, hDT, hDh, smul_eq_mul, smul_eq_mul,
        smul_eq_mul, smul_eq_mul, hT]
      simp only [map_sub, map_intCast, map_natCast, q]
      field_simp
      ring

private theorem ord_prod {ι : Type*} (P : Pt) (s : Finset ι) (f : ι → K) (hf : ∀ i ∈ s, f i ≠ 0) :
    C.ord P (∏ i ∈ s, f i) = ∑ i ∈ s, C.ord P (f i) := by
  classical
  induction s using Finset.induction_on with
  | empty => simp [C.ord_one]
  | insert a s ha ih =>
    rw [Finset.prod_insert ha, Finset.sum_insert ha,
      C.ord_mul P _ _ (hf a (Finset.mem_insert_self a s))
        (Finset.prod_ne_zero_iff.mpr fun i hi => hf i (Finset.mem_insert_of_mem hi)),
      ih fun i hi => hf i (Finset.mem_insert_of_mem hi)]

end CurveFF

/-- The Wronskian `det (D^j f_i)` of a family of functions. -/
private noncomputable def wronskian {k K : Type*} [Field k] [Field K] [Algebra k K]
    (D : Derivation k K K) {r : ℕ} (f : Fin r → K) : K :=
  Matrix.det (Matrix.of fun i j : Fin r => (⇑D)^[(j : ℕ)] (f i))

namespace CurveFF

/-- The polynomial `∏_{l < j} (X - l + l e)`. -/
private noncomputable def wPoly (e : ℤ) (j : ℕ) : Polynomial k :=
  ∏ l ∈ Finset.range j, (Polynomial.X - Polynomial.C ((l : k) - l * e))

omit [Field K] [Algebra k K] in
private theorem wPoly_monic (e : ℤ) (j : ℕ) : (wPoly (k := k) e j).Monic :=
  Polynomial.monic_prod_of_monic _ _ fun l _ => Polynomial.monic_X_sub_C _

omit [Field K] [Algebra k K] in
private theorem wPoly_natDegree [Nontrivial k] (e : ℤ) (j : ℕ) :
    (wPoly (k := k) e j).natDegree = j := by
  rw [wPoly, Polynomial.natDegree_prod_of_monic _ _ fun l _ => Polynomial.monic_X_sub_C _,
    Finset.sum_congr rfl fun l _ => Polynomial.natDegree_X_sub_C _]
  simp

omit [Field K] [Algebra k K] in
private theorem wPoly_eval (e : ℤ) (j : ℕ) (a : ℤ) :
    (wPoly (k := k) e j).eval (a : k) = ∏ l ∈ Finset.range j, ((a : k) - l + l * e) := by
  rw [wPoly, Polynomial.eval_prod]
  refine Finset.prod_congr rfl fun l _ => ?_
  simp; ring

variable (D : Derivation k K K)

/-- **The order of a Wronskian.** For nonzero functions `f_i` with pairwise distinct orders at
`P`, `ord_P W_D(f) = ∑ ord_P f_i + (∑_{j < r} j) (ord_P (D t) - 1)`. -/
private theorem ord_wronskian [CharZero k] {P : Pt} {t : K} (ht : C.ord P t = 1) (hD : D t ≠ 0)
    (hDO : ∀ u ∈ C.valRing P, D u = 0 ∨ C.ord P (D t) ≤ C.ord P (D u)) {r : ℕ} (f : Fin r → K)
    (hf : ∀ i, f i ≠ 0) (hinj : Function.Injective fun i => C.ord P (f i)) :
    wronskian D f ≠ 0 ∧ C.ord P (wronskian D f) =
      ∑ i, C.ord P (f i) + (∑ j : Fin r, (j : ℤ)) * (C.ord P (D t) - 1) := by
  classical
  have ht0 := C.ne_zero_of_ord_eq_one ht
  set h := D t
  set e := C.ord P h
  set a : Fin r → ℤ := fun i => C.ord P (f i)
  set u : Fin r → K := fun i => f i / t ^ a i
  have hta : ∀ i, t ^ a i ≠ 0 := fun i => zpow_ne_zero _ ht0
  have hfu : ∀ i, f i = t ^ a i * u i := fun i => by simp only [u]; field_simp
  have hu0 : ∀ i, u i ≠ 0 := fun i => div_ne_zero (hf i) (hta i)
  have huord : ∀ i, C.ord P (u i) = 0 := fun i => by
    simp only [u]; rw [C.ord_div P (hf i) (hta i), C.ord_zpow P ht0, ht]; simp [a]
  have huO : ∀ i, u i ∈ C.valRing P := fun i => Or.inr (by rw [huord])
  have hures : ∀ i, C.res P ⟨u i, huO i⟩ ≠ 0 := fun i hres => by
    rcases (C.res_eq_zero_iff _).mp hres with h0 | h1
    · exact hu0 i h0
    · have := huord i; simp at h1; omega
  have huc : ∀ i, C.IsRes P (u i) (C.res P ⟨u i, huO i⟩) := fun i => C.isRes_res P ⟨u i, huO i⟩
  have hw := fun i (j : Fin r) =>
    C.iterate_derivation_zpow_mul D ht hD hDO (a i) (huc i) (j : ℕ)
  choose w hwres hweq using hw
  have hwO : ∀ i j, w i j ∈ C.valRing P := fun i j => C.mem_valRing_of_isRes (hwres i j)
  let wO : Matrix (Fin r) (Fin r) (C.valRing P) := Matrix.of fun i j => ⟨w i j, hwO i j⟩
  have hdetw : ((wO.det : C.valRing P) : K) = Matrix.det (Matrix.of fun i j => w i j) := by
    have := RingHom.map_det (C.valRing P).subtype wO
    simpa [wO, Matrix.map] using this
  have hresdet : C.res P wO.det = (∏ i, C.res P ⟨u i, huO i⟩) *
      Matrix.det (Matrix.vandermonde fun i => ((a i : ℤ) : k)) := by
    rw [RingHom.map_det]
    have : (C.res P).mapMatrix wO = Matrix.of fun (i j : Fin r) =>
        C.res P ⟨u i, huO i⟩ * (wPoly (k := k) e (j : ℕ)).eval ((a i : ℤ) : k) := by
      ext i j
      simp only [RingHom.mapMatrix_apply, Matrix.map_apply, wO, Matrix.of_apply]
      rw [C.res_eq_of_isRes (hwres i j), wPoly_eval]; ring
    have h5 := Matrix.det_mul_column (fun i => C.res P ⟨u i, huO i⟩)
      (Matrix.of fun (i j : Fin r) => (wPoly (k := k) e (j : ℕ)).eval ((a i : ℤ) : k))
    simp only [Matrix.of_apply] at h5
    rw [this, h5,
      Matrix.det_eval_matrixOfPolynomials_eq_det_vandermonde _ (fun j : Fin r => wPoly e (j : ℕ))
        (fun j => wPoly_natDegree e j) (fun j => wPoly_monic e j)]
  have hvan : Matrix.det (Matrix.vandermonde fun i => ((a i : ℤ) : k)) ≠ 0 :=
    Matrix.det_vandermonde_ne_zero_iff.mpr fun i i' hii => hinj (by exact_mod_cast hii)
  have hres0 : C.res P wO.det ≠ 0 := by
    rw [hresdet]
    exact mul_ne_zero (Finset.prod_ne_zero_iff.mpr fun i _ => hures i) hvan
  have hordw : C.ord P (wO.det : K) = 0 := C.ord_eq_zero_of_res_ne_zero _ hres0
  have hw0 : (wO.det : K) ≠ 0 := fun h0 => hres0 ((C.res_eq_zero_iff _).mpr (Or.inl h0))
  have hmat : (Matrix.of fun i j : Fin r => (⇑D)^[(j : ℕ)] (f i)) =
      Matrix.of fun (i j : Fin r) => t ^ a i * ((h * t⁻¹) ^ (j : ℕ) * w i j) := by
    ext i j
    simp only [Matrix.of_apply]
    rw [hfu i, hweq i j, zpow_sub₀ ht0, zpow_natCast, mul_pow, inv_pow]
    field_simp
    ring
  have hW : wronskian D f = (∏ i, t ^ a i) * ((∏ j : Fin r, (h * t⁻¹) ^ (j : ℕ)) *
      (wO.det : K)) := by
    unfold wronskian
    have h5 := Matrix.det_mul_column (fun i => t ^ a i)
      (Matrix.of fun (i j : Fin r) => (h * t⁻¹) ^ (j : ℕ) * w i j)
    have h6 := Matrix.det_mul_row (fun j : Fin r => (h * t⁻¹) ^ (j : ℕ))
      (Matrix.of fun (i j : Fin r) => w i j)
    simp only [Matrix.of_apply] at h5 h6
    rw [hmat, h5, h6, hdetw]
  have hht : h * t⁻¹ ≠ 0 := mul_ne_zero hD (inv_ne_zero ht0)
  have hp1 : (∏ i, t ^ a i) ≠ 0 := Finset.prod_ne_zero_iff.mpr fun i _ => hta i
  have hp2 : (∏ j : Fin r, (h * t⁻¹) ^ (j : ℕ)) ≠ 0 :=
    Finset.prod_ne_zero_iff.mpr fun j _ => pow_ne_zero _ hht
  refine ⟨by rw [hW]; exact mul_ne_zero hp1 (mul_ne_zero hp2 hw0), ?_⟩
  rw [hW, C.ord_mul P _ _ hp1 (mul_ne_zero hp2 hw0), C.ord_mul P _ _ hp2 hw0, hordw, add_zero,
    C.ord_prod P _ _ (fun i _ => hta i), C.ord_prod P _ _ (fun j _ => pow_ne_zero _ hht)]
  simp only [C.ord_zpow P ht0, ht, mul_one, C.ord_pow P hht, C.ord_mul P _ _ hD (inv_ne_zero ht0),
    C.ord_inv P ht0]
  rw [Finset.sum_mul]
  rfl

end CurveFF

private theorem wronskian_linear_comb {k K : Type*} [Field k] [Field K] [Algebra k K]
    (D : Derivation k K K) {r : ℕ} (g : Fin r → K) (A : Matrix (Fin r) (Fin r) k) :
    wronskian D (fun i => ∑ l, A i l • g l) = algebraMap k K A.det * wronskian D g := by
  unfold wronskian
  have hlin : ∀ (j : ℕ) (x : K), (⇑D)^[j] x = ((D : K →ₗ[k] K) ^ j) x := fun j x => by
    rw [Module.End.pow_apply]; rfl
  have : (Matrix.of fun i j : Fin r => (⇑D)^[(j : ℕ)] (∑ l, A i l • g l)) =
      (A.map (algebraMap k K)) * Matrix.of fun i j : Fin r => (⇑D)^[(j : ℕ)] (g i) := by
    ext i j
    simp only [Matrix.of_apply, Matrix.mul_apply, Matrix.map_apply, hlin, map_sum, map_smul]
    simp only [Algebra.smul_def]
  rw [this, Matrix.det_mul, ← RingHom.mapMatrix_apply, ← RingHom.map_det]

namespace CurveFF

/-- The finite set of orders of a finite-dimensional subspace, as a `Finset`. -/
private noncomputable def ordFinset (P : Pt) (L : Submodule k K) [FiniteDimensional k L] :
    Finset ℤ :=
  (C.ordSet_finite_and_ncard P _ L rfl).1.toFinset

private theorem mem_ordFinset {P : Pt} {L : Submodule k K} [FiniteDimensional k L] {a : ℤ} :
    a ∈ C.ordFinset P L ↔ ∃ f ∈ L, f ≠ 0 ∧ C.ord P f = a := by
  simp [ordFinset, ordSet]

private theorem card_ordFinset (P : Pt) (L : Submodule k K) [FiniteDimensional k L] :
    (C.ordFinset P L).card = finrank k L := by
  rw [ordFinset, ← Set.ncard_eq_toFinset_card _ (C.ordSet_finite_and_ncard P _ L rfl).1]
  exact (C.ordSet_finite_and_ncard P _ L rfl).2

/-- An adapted basis at `P`: elements of `L` with pairwise distinct orders. -/
private theorem exists_adapted (P : Pt) (L : Submodule k K) [FiniteDimensional k L] :
    ∃ g : Fin (finrank k L) → K, (∀ i, g i ∈ L) ∧ (∀ i, g i ≠ 0) ∧
      Function.Injective (fun i => C.ord P (g i)) ∧
      ∀ a, a ∈ C.ordFinset P L ↔ ∃ i, C.ord P (g i) = a := by
  classical
  let e : Fin (finrank k L) ≃ C.ordFinset P L :=
    (Finset.equivFinOfCardEq (C.card_ordFinset P L)).symm
  have hch : ∀ a : C.ordFinset P L, ∃ f ∈ L, f ≠ 0 ∧ C.ord P f = a := fun a =>
    (C.mem_ordFinset).mp a.2
  choose f hfL hf0 hford using hch
  refine ⟨fun i => f (e i), fun i => hfL _, fun i => hf0 _, fun i i' h => ?_, fun a => ?_⟩
  · have : (e i : ℤ) = e i' := by simpa [hford] using h
    exact e.injective (Subtype.ext this)
  · constructor
    · intro ha
      exact ⟨e.symm ⟨a, ha⟩, by simp [hford]⟩
    · rintro ⟨i, rfl⟩
      rw [hford]; exact (e i).2

variable (D : Derivation k K K)

/-- **The order of the Wronskian of a basis.** For a basis `g` of a finite-dimensional subspace
`L`, `W_D(g) ≠ 0` and `ord_P W_D(g) = ∑_{a} a + (∑_{j < r} j)(ord_P (D t) - 1)`, the first sum
over the orders at `P` of the nonzero elements of `L`. -/
private theorem ord_wronskian_basis [CharZero k] {P : Pt} {t : K} (ht : C.ord P t = 1)
    (hD : D t ≠ 0)
    (hDO : ∀ u ∈ C.valRing P, D u = 0 ∨ C.ord P (D t) ≤ C.ord P (D u))
    (L : Submodule k K) [FiniteDimensional k L] (b : Module.Basis (Fin (finrank k L)) k L) :
    wronskian D (fun i => (b i : K)) ≠ 0 ∧ C.ord P (wronskian D fun i => (b i : K)) =
      ∑ a ∈ C.ordFinset P L, a +
        (∑ j : Fin (finrank k L), (j : ℤ)) * (C.ord P (D t) - 1) := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨g, hgL, hg0, hginj, hgset⟩ := C.exists_adapted P L
  set A : Matrix (Fin (finrank k L)) (Fin (finrank k L)) k :=
    Matrix.of fun i l => b.repr ⟨g i, hgL i⟩ l
  have hg : g = fun i => ∑ l, A i l • (b l : K) := by
    funext i
    have h := congrArg Subtype.val (b.sum_repr ⟨g i, hgL i⟩)
    simp only [Submodule.coe_sum, Submodule.coe_smul] at h
    exact h.symm
  obtain ⟨hW0, hWord⟩ := C.ord_wronskian D ht hD hDO g hg0 hginj
  have hlin := wronskian_linear_comb D (fun i => (b i : K)) A
  rw [← hg] at hlin
  have hdet : A.det ≠ 0 := fun h0 => hW0 (by rw [hlin, h0, map_zero, zero_mul])
  have hWb : wronskian D (fun i => (b i : K)) ≠ 0 := fun h0 => hW0 (by rw [hlin, h0, mul_zero])
  refine ⟨hWb, ?_⟩
  have h1 : C.ord P (wronskian D g) = C.ord P (wronskian D fun i => (b i : K)) := by
    rw [hlin, C.ord_mul P _ _ (by simpa using hdet) hWb, C.ord_algebraMap P _ hdet, zero_add]
  rw [← h1, hWord]
  congr 1
  have himg : Finset.univ.image (fun i => C.ord P (g i)) = C.ordFinset P L := by
    ext a
    simp only [Finset.mem_image, Finset.mem_univ, true_and]
    exact (hgset a).symm
  rw [← himg, Finset.sum_image fun i _ i' _ h => hginj h]

end CurveFF

/-- A curve function field with a nonzero derivation `D` and a canonical divisor `κ` of degree
`2g - 2`, such that at each point, for a uniformizer `t`, `ord_P (D t) = -κ_P` and
`D 𝒪_P ⊆ (D t) 𝒪_P`. (For `D` dual to a rational differential `ω`, `κ = div ω`.) -/
private structure CurveFFDer (k K Pt : Type*) [Field k] [Field K] [Algebra k K]
    extends CurveFFRR k K Pt where
  canon : Pt →₀ ℤ
  deg_canon : ProperCurveFF.deg canon = 2 * (genus : ℤ) - 2
  der : Derivation k K K
  der_loc : ∀ P, ∃ t : K, ord P t = 1 ∧ der t ≠ 0 ∧ ord P (der t) = -canon P ∧
    ∀ u : K, (u = 0 ∨ 0 ≤ ord P u) → der u = 0 ∨ ord P (der t) ≤ ord P (der u)

namespace CurveFFDer

variable (C : CurveFFDer k K Pt)

open ProperCurveFF

/-- The orders `ord_P f + D_P`, `f ∈ L(D)` nonzero. -/
private noncomputable def shifted (Dv : Pt →₀ ℤ) (P : Pt) : Finset ℤ :=
  (C.ordFinset P (C.lin Dv)).image (· + Dv P)

/-- The weight of the linear system `L(D)` at `P`. -/
private noncomputable def weight (Dv : Pt →₀ ℤ) (P : Pt) : ℤ :=
  ∑ x ∈ C.shifted Dv P, x - ∑ j : Fin (finrank k (C.lin Dv)), (j : ℤ)

private theorem card_shifted (Dv : Pt →₀ ℤ) (P : Pt) :
    (C.shifted Dv P).card = finrank k (C.lin Dv) := by
  rw [shifted, Finset.card_image_of_injective _ (add_left_injective _), C.card_ordFinset]

private theorem sum_shifted (Dv : Pt →₀ ℤ) (P : Pt) :
    ∑ x ∈ C.shifted Dv P, x = ∑ a ∈ C.ordFinset P (C.lin Dv), a +
      finrank k (C.lin Dv) * Dv P := by
  rw [shifted, Finset.sum_image fun a _ b _ h => add_right_cancel h, Finset.sum_add_distrib,
    Finset.sum_const, C.card_ordFinset, nsmul_eq_mul]

private theorem mem_shifted_bounds {Dv : Pt →₀ ℤ} {P : Pt} {x : ℤ} (hx : x ∈ C.shifted Dv P) :
    0 ≤ x ∧ x ≤ deg Dv := by
  obtain ⟨a, ha, rfl⟩ := Finset.mem_image.mp hx
  obtain ⟨f, hf, hf0, rfl⟩ := C.mem_ordFinset.mp ha
  refine ⟨?_, C.ord_add_le_deg hf hf0 P⟩
  rcases hf with h | h
  · exact absurd h hf0
  · exact h P

/-- The Wronskian of the linear system `L(D)` with respect to a basis. -/
private noncomputable def wr (Dv : Pt →₀ ℤ) : K :=
  wronskian C.der fun i => ((Module.finBasis k (C.lin Dv) i : C.lin Dv) : K)

private theorem wr_ne_zero_and_ord [CharZero k] (Dv : Pt →₀ ℤ) (P : Pt) :
    C.wr Dv ≠ 0 ∧ C.ord P (C.wr Dv) = ∑ a ∈ C.ordFinset P (C.lin Dv), a +
      (∑ j : Fin (finrank k (C.lin Dv)), (j : ℤ)) * (-C.canon P - 1) := by
  obtain ⟨t, ht, hD, hDt, hDO⟩ := C.der_loc P
  have := C.ord_wronskian_basis C.der ht hD hDO (C.lin Dv)
    (Module.finBasis k (C.lin Dv))
  rwa [hDt] at this

private theorem wr_ne_zero [CharZero k] (Dv : Pt →₀ ℤ) : C.wr Dv ≠ 0 := by
  obtain ⟨P⟩ := C.nonempty
  exact (C.wr_ne_zero_and_ord Dv P).1

/-- The weight divisor `div W + r D + (∑ j) κ`, whose coefficients are the weights. -/
private noncomputable def weightDiv [CharZero k] (Dv : Pt →₀ ℤ) : Pt →₀ ℤ :=
  C.div (C.wr Dv) (C.wr_ne_zero Dv) + ((finrank k (C.lin Dv) : ℤ) • Dv) +
    (∑ j : Fin (finrank k (C.lin Dv)), (j : ℤ)) • C.canon

private theorem weightDiv_apply [CharZero k] (Dv : Pt →₀ ℤ) (P : Pt) :
    C.weightDiv Dv P = C.weight Dv P := by
  simp only [weightDiv, Finsupp.add_apply, div_apply, Finsupp.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul, weight,
    sum_shifted, (C.wr_ne_zero_and_ord Dv P).2]
  ring

private theorem deg_weightDiv [CharZero k] (Dv : Pt →₀ ℤ) :
    deg (C.weightDiv Dv) = finrank k (C.lin Dv) * deg Dv +
      (∑ j : Fin (finrank k (C.lin Dv)), (j : ℤ)) * (2 * (C.genus : ℤ) - 2) := by
  rw [weightDiv, deg_add, deg_add, deg_div_eq_zero, deg_smul, deg_smul, C.deg_canon, zero_add]

private theorem sum_range_le_sum_of_nonneg (T : Finset ℤ) (h : ∀ x ∈ T, 0 ≤ x) :
    ∑ j ∈ Finset.range T.card, (j : ℤ) ≤ ∑ x ∈ T, x := by
  induction T using Finset.induction_on_max with
  | empty => simp
  | insert a T ha ih =>
    have haT : a ∉ T := fun h' => lt_irrefl a (ha a h')
    rw [Finset.card_insert_of_notMem haT, Finset.sum_range_succ, Finset.sum_insert haT]
    have h1 := ih fun x hx => h x (Finset.mem_insert_of_mem hx)
    have hsub : T ⊆ Finset.Ico 0 a := fun x hx => Finset.mem_Ico.mpr
      ⟨h x (Finset.mem_insert_of_mem hx), ha x hx⟩
    have h2 := Finset.card_le_card hsub
    rw [Int.card_Ico, sub_zero] at h2
    have h3 : (T.card : ℤ) ≤ a := by
      have := h a (Finset.mem_insert_self a T)
      omega
    linarith

private theorem sum_le_card_mul_sub_sum_range (T : Finset ℤ) (N : ℤ) (h : ∀ x ∈ T, x ≤ N) :
    ∑ x ∈ T, x ≤ T.card * N - ∑ j ∈ Finset.range T.card, (j : ℤ) := by
  have := sum_range_le_sum_of_nonneg (T.image (N - ·)) fun y hy => by
    obtain ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩ := Finset.mem_image.mp hy; have := h x hx; omega
  rw [Finset.card_image_of_injective _ (sub_right_injective), Finset.sum_image
    (fun x _ y _ hxy => sub_right_injective hxy), Finset.sum_sub_distrib, Finset.sum_const,
    nsmul_eq_mul] at this
  linarith

private theorem two_mul_sum_fin_eq (r : ℕ) : 2 * ∑ j : Fin r, (j : ℤ) = r * (r - 1) := by
  rw [Fin.sum_univ_eq_sum_range (fun j => (j : ℤ)) r]
  have := Finset.sum_range_id_mul_two r
  have h2 : (∑ j ∈ Finset.range r, (j : ℤ)) = ((∑ j ∈ Finset.range r, j : ℕ) : ℤ) := by
    push_cast; rfl
  rw [h2]
  rcases r with _ | r
  · simp
  · have : ((∑ i ∈ Finset.range (r + 1), i) * 2 : ℕ) = (r + 1) * r := by simpa using this
    have h3 : (((∑ i ∈ Finset.range (r + 1), i : ℕ) : ℤ)) * 2 = ((r + 1) * r : ℕ) := by
      exact_mod_cast this
    push_cast at h3 ⊢
    linarith

private theorem weight_nonneg_and_le (Dv : Pt →₀ ℤ) (P : Pt) :
    0 ≤ C.weight Dv P ∧ C.weight Dv P ≤
      finrank k (C.lin Dv) * deg Dv - 2 * ∑ j : Fin (finrank k (C.lin Dv)), (j : ℤ) := by
  have hlow := sum_range_le_sum_of_nonneg (C.shifted Dv P) fun x hx =>
    (C.mem_shifted_bounds hx).1
  have hup := sum_le_card_mul_sub_sum_range (C.shifted Dv P) (deg Dv) fun x hx => (C.mem_shifted_bounds hx).2
  rw [C.card_shifted] at hlow hup
  rw [← Fin.sum_univ_eq_sum_range (fun j => (j : ℤ))] at hlow hup
  unfold weight
  constructor <;> linarith

/-- Counting the points where an effective divisor bounded by `M` is positive. -/
private theorem deg_le_mul_ncard {E : Pt →₀ ℤ} (hE : ∀ P, 0 ≤ E P) {M : ℤ} (hM : ∀ P, E P ≤ M) :
    {P | 1 ≤ E P}.Finite ∧ deg E ≤ M * {P | 1 ≤ E P}.ncard := by
  classical
  have hset : {P | 1 ≤ E P} = ↑E.support := by
    ext P; simp only [Set.mem_setOf_eq, Finset.mem_coe, Finsupp.mem_support_iff]
    have := hE P; omega
  rw [hset, Set.ncard_coe_finset]
  refine ⟨Finset.finite_toSet _, ?_⟩
  calc deg E = ∑ P ∈ E.support, E P := rfl
    _ ≤ ∑ P ∈ E.support, M := Finset.sum_le_sum fun P _ => hM P
    _ = M * E.support.card := by rw [Finset.sum_const, nsmul_eq_mul, mul_comm]

/-- **Invariance of the weight.** If `σ` permutes the points through `π` and `D_{π P} =
ord_P c + D_P` for some nonzero `c`, then `f ↦ σ f · c` preserves `L(D)` and the weights. -/
private theorem weight_eq_of_twist {σ : K ≃ₐ[k] K} {π π' : Pt → Pt} (h : C.IsPointMap σ π)
    (h' : C.IsPointMap σ⁻¹ π') {Dv : Pt →₀ ℤ} {c : K} (hc : c ≠ 0)
    (hcD : ∀ P, C.ord P c + Dv P = Dv (π P)) (P : Pt) :
    C.weight Dv P = C.weight Dv (π P) := by
  have hpp : ∀ Q, π (π' Q) = Q := fun Q => congrFun (CurveFFRR.IsPointMap.inv_comp _ h h') Q
  have hset : C.shifted Dv P = C.shifted Dv (π P) := by
    ext x
    simp only [shifted, Finset.mem_image, C.mem_ordFinset]
    constructor
    · rintro ⟨_, ⟨f, hf, hf0, rfl⟩, rfl⟩
      set f' := σ⁻¹ (f / c)
      have hσf' : σ f' * c = f := by
        simp only [f']; rw [show σ (σ⁻¹ (f / c)) = f / c from σ.apply_symm_apply _]
        field_simp
      have hf'0 : f' ≠ 0 := by
        simp only [f']; rw [map_ne_zero_iff _ (σ⁻¹).injective]; exact div_ne_zero hf0 hc
      refine ⟨_, ⟨f', ?_, hf'0, rfl⟩, ?_⟩
      · right; intro Q
        have e1 : C.ord Q f' = C.ord (π' Q) (f / c) := h' Q _
        have e2 := hcD (π' Q)
        rw [hpp] at e2
        rw [e1, C.ord_div _ hf0 hc]
        rcases hf with hf | hf
        · exact absurd hf hf0
        · have := hf (π' Q); omega
      · have e1 : C.ord P f = C.ord (π P) f' + C.ord P c := by
          rw [← hσf', C.ord_mul P _ _ (by simpa using hf'0) hc, h P]
        have e2 := hcD P
        omega
    · rintro ⟨_, ⟨f, hf, hf0, rfl⟩, rfl⟩
      have hσf0 : σ f * c ≠ 0 := mul_ne_zero (by simpa using hf0) hc
      refine ⟨_, ⟨σ f * c, ?_, hσf0, rfl⟩, ?_⟩
      · right; intro Q
        rw [C.ord_mul Q _ _ (by simpa using hf0) hc, h Q]
        have := hcD Q
        rcases hf with hf | hf
        · exact absurd hf hf0
        · have := hf (π Q); omega
      · rw [C.ord_mul P _ _ (by simpa using hf0) hc, h P]
        have := hcD P; omega
  unfold weight
  rw [hset]

/-- **Finiteness of the automorphisms preserving a large linear system.** On a curve of genus
`g ≥ 1`, the automorphisms of the function field which permute the points and preserve, up to a
twist, a divisor `D` of degree at least `3 g + 2`, form a finite set. -/
private theorem finite_of_twist [CharZero k] (hg : 1 ≤ C.genus) {Dv : Pt →₀ ℤ}
    (hN : 3 * (C.genus : ℤ) + 2 ≤ deg Dv) (G : Set (K ≃ₐ[k] K))
    (π π' : (K ≃ₐ[k] K) → Pt → Pt)
    (hG : ∀ σ ∈ G, C.IsPointMap σ (π σ) ∧ C.IsPointMap σ⁻¹ (π' σ) ∧
      ∃ c : K, c ≠ 0 ∧ ∀ P, C.ord P c + Dv P = Dv (π σ P)) : G.Finite := by
  classical
  set S := {P | 1 ≤ C.weightDiv Dv P}
  set r := finrank k (C.lin Dv)
  set N := deg Dv
  set sj := ∑ j : Fin r, (j : ℤ)
  have hsj : 2 * sj = r * (r - 1) := two_mul_sum_fin_eq r
  have hbounds := C.weight_nonneg_and_le Dv
  obtain ⟨hSfin, hcount⟩ := deg_le_mul_ncard (E := C.weightDiv Dv)
    (fun P => by rw [weightDiv_apply]; exact (hbounds P).1)
    (fun P => by rw [weightDiv_apply]; exact (hbounds P).2)
  rw [deg_weightDiv] at hcount
  have hrr : N + 1 - C.genus ≤ (r : ℤ) := C.rr Dv
  set nS := (S.ncard : ℤ)
  have hnS : 2 * ((C.genus : ℤ) + 1) < nS := by
    by_contra hcon
    push Not at hcon
    have hg' : (1 : ℤ) ≤ C.genus := by exact_mod_cast hg
    have hr1 : (1 : ℤ) ≤ r := by linarith
    have hnS0 : (0 : ℤ) ≤ nS := by positivity
    set e := N - r + 1
    have he : e ≤ C.genus := by linarith
    have hcount' : (r : ℤ) * N + r * (r - 1) * (C.genus - 1) ≤ (r * N - r * (r - 1)) * nS := by
      have : (r : ℤ) * N + sj * (2 * C.genus - 2) = r * N + (2 * sj) * (C.genus - 1) := by ring
      rw [hsj] at this
      have h2 : (r : ℤ) * N - 2 * sj = r * N - r * (r - 1) := by rw [hsj]
      rw [← this, ← h2]; exact hcount
    have hfac : (r : ℤ) * N - r * (r - 1) = r * e := by simp only [e]; ring
    rw [hfac] at hcount'
    have hdiv : (N : ℤ) + (r - 1) * (C.genus - 1) ≤ e * nS := by
      have : (r : ℤ) * (N + (r - 1) * (C.genus - 1)) ≤ r * (e * nS) := by nlinarith
      exact le_of_mul_le_mul_left this (by linarith)
    rcases le_or_gt e 0 with he0 | he0
    · have : e * nS ≤ 0 := mul_nonpos_of_nonpos_of_nonneg he0 hnS0
      nlinarith
    · have h1 : e * nS ≤ e * (2 * (C.genus + 1)) := mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left hcon he0.le
      have hre : (r : ℤ) - 1 = N - e := by simp only [e]; ring
      rw [hre] at hdiv
      nlinarith
  refine C.finite_of_mapsTo G π π' hSfin hnS fun σ hσ => ?_
  obtain ⟨h1, h2, c, hc, hcD⟩ := hG σ hσ
  refine ⟨h1, h2, fun P hP => ?_⟩
  simp only [S, Set.mem_setOf_eq, weightDiv_apply] at hP ⊢
  rwa [← C.weight_eq_of_twist h1 h2 hc hcD P]

private theorem intCast_ne_zero_K [CharZero k] {a : ℤ} (ha : a ≠ 0) : (a : K) ≠ 0 := by
  rw [← map_intCast (algebraMap k K)]
  exact (map_ne_zero_iff _ (algebraMap k K).injective).mpr (Int.cast_ne_zero.mpr ha)

private theorem ord_intCast [CharZero k] (P : Pt) {a : ℤ} (ha : a ≠ 0) : C.ord P (a : K) = 0 := by
  rw [← map_intCast (algebraMap k K)]
  exact C.ord_algebraMap P _ (Int.cast_ne_zero.mpr ha)

/-- Derivatives of functions without pole have order at least `-κ_P`. -/
private theorem der_eq_zero_or_le {P : Pt} {f : K} (hf : f = 0 ∨ 0 ≤ C.ord P f) :
    C.der f = 0 ∨ -C.canon P ≤ C.ord P (C.der f) := by
  obtain ⟨t, ht, hD, hDt, hDO⟩ := C.der_loc P
  rcases hDO f hf with h | h
  · exact Or.inl h
  · exact Or.inr (hDt ▸ h)

/-- **The order of a derivative.** If `ord_P f = a ≠ 0` then `ord_P (D f) = a - 1 - κ_P`. -/
private theorem ord_der_of_ne_zero [CharZero k] {P : Pt} {f : K} (hf : f ≠ 0) (ha : C.ord P f ≠ 0) :
    C.der f ≠ 0 ∧ C.ord P (C.der f) = C.ord P f - 1 - C.canon P := by
  obtain ⟨t, ht, hD, hDt, hDO⟩ := C.der_loc P
  have ht0 := C.ne_zero_of_ord_eq_one ht
  set a := C.ord P f
  set u := f / t ^ a
  have hta : t ^ a ≠ 0 := zpow_ne_zero _ ht0
  have hu0 : u ≠ 0 := div_ne_zero hf hta
  have huord : C.ord P u = 0 := by
    simp only [u]; rw [C.ord_div P hf hta, C.ord_zpow P ht0, ht]; ring
  have hfu : f = t ^ a * u := by simp only [u]; field_simp
  have hDf : C.der f = (a : K) * t ^ (a - 1) * u * C.der t + t ^ a * C.der u := by
    conv_lhs => rw [hfu]
    rw [Derivation.leibniz, Derivation.leibniz_zpow' C.der t, smul_eq_mul, smul_eq_mul]; ring
  have hX0 : (a : K) * t ^ (a - 1) * u * C.der t ≠ 0 :=
    mul_ne_zero (mul_ne_zero (mul_ne_zero (intCast_ne_zero_K (k := k) ha) (zpow_ne_zero _ ht0))
      hu0) hD
  have hXord : C.ord P ((a : K) * t ^ (a - 1) * u * C.der t) = a - 1 - C.canon P := by
    rw [C.ord_mul P _ _ (mul_ne_zero (mul_ne_zero (intCast_ne_zero_K (k := k) ha)
      (zpow_ne_zero _ ht0)) hu0) hD, C.ord_mul P _ _ (mul_ne_zero (intCast_ne_zero_K (k := k) ha)
      (zpow_ne_zero _ ht0)) hu0, C.ord_mul P _ _ (intCast_ne_zero_K (k := k) ha)
      (zpow_ne_zero _ ht0),
      C.ord_intCast P ha, C.ord_zpow P ht0, ht, huord, hDt]
    ring
  by_cases hY0 : C.der u = 0
  · rw [hDf, hY0, mul_zero, add_zero]; exact ⟨hX0, hXord⟩
  rcases hDO u (Or.inr huord.ge) with hY | hY
  · exact absurd hY hY0
  have hYord : C.ord P (t ^ a * C.der u) = a + C.ord P (C.der u) := by
    rw [C.ord_mul P _ _ hta hY0, C.ord_zpow P ht0, ht, mul_one]
  have hlt : C.ord P ((a : K) * t ^ (a - 1) * u * C.der t) < C.ord P (t ^ a * C.der u) := by
    rw [hXord, hYord]; rw [hDt] at hY; omega
  rw [hDf]
  exact ⟨C.add_ne_zero_of_ord_ne P hX0 hlt.ne,
    (C.ord_add_eq_of_lt P hX0 (mul_ne_zero hta hY0) hlt).trans hXord⟩

/-- In genus at least one no function has a single simple pole. -/
private theorem const_of_mem_lin_single [CharZero k] (hg : 1 ≤ C.genus) (P : Pt) {f : K}
    (hf : f ∈ C.lin (Finsupp.single P 1)) : ∃ c : k, f = algebraMap k K c := by
  classical
  by_contra hfc
  push Not at hfc
  have hf0 : f ≠ 0 := fun h => hfc 0 (by rw [h, map_zero])
  rcases hf with h | hf
  · exact hf0 h
  have hQ : ∀ Q, Q ≠ P → 0 ≤ C.ord Q f := fun Q hQ => by
    have := hf Q; rwa [Finsupp.single_eq_of_ne hQ, add_zero] at this
  have hP1 : -1 ≤ C.ord P f := by have := hf P; simp at this; omega
  have hP : C.ord P f = -1 := by
    by_contra hne
    obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := C.const f fun Q => by
      by_cases hQP : Q = P
      · rw [hQP]; omega
      · exact hQ Q hQP
    exact hfc c hc
  have hDP := C.ord_der_of_ne_zero hf0 (by rw [hP]; omega)
  have hDQ : ∀ Q, Q ≠ P → C.ord Q (C.der f) = -C.canon Q := by
    intro Q hQP
    obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := C.residue Q f (hQ Q hQP)
    rcases hc with hc | hc
    · exact absurd hc (hfc c)
    set g := f - algebraMap k K c
    have hg0 : g ≠ 0 := fun h => hfc c (by linear_combination h)
    have hgP : C.ord P g = -1 := by
      rw [C.ord_sub_algebraMap_of_neg P hf0 (by omega), hP]
    have hE : ∀ Q', 0 ≤ (C.div g hg0 + Finsupp.single P (1 : ℤ) : Pt →₀ ℤ) Q' := fun Q' => by
      simp only [Finsupp.add_apply, div_apply, Finsupp.single_apply]
      by_cases hQ' : P = Q'
      · subst hQ'; rw [if_pos rfl, hgP]; omega
      · rw [if_neg hQ', add_zero]
        exact C.ord_sub_algebraMap_nonneg Q' (hQ Q' (Ne.symm hQ')) hg0
    have hle := le_deg_of_nonneg hE Q
    rw [deg_add, C.deg_div_eq_zero, deg_single] at hle
    have hs : (Finsupp.single P (1 : ℤ)) Q = 0 := by
      simp [Finsupp.single_apply, Ne.symm hQP]
    simp only [Finsupp.add_apply, div_apply, hs, add_zero] at hle
    have hgQ : C.ord Q g = 1 := by omega
    have hDg := C.ord_der_of_ne_zero hg0 (by rw [hgQ]; omega)
    have hDfg : C.der f = C.der g := by
      simp only [g, map_sub, Derivation.map_algebraMap, sub_zero]
    rw [hDfg, hDg.2, hgQ]; ring
  have hdiv : C.div (C.der f) hDP.1 = -C.canon - Finsupp.single P 2 := by
    ext Q
    simp only [div_apply, Finsupp.sub_apply, Finsupp.neg_apply, Finsupp.single_apply]
    by_cases hQP : P = Q
    · subst hQP; rw [if_pos rfl, hDP.2, hP]; ring
    · rw [if_neg hQP, hDQ Q (Ne.symm hQP)]; ring
  have h1 := C.deg_div_eq_zero (C.der f) hDP.1
  rw [hdiv, sub_eq_add_neg, deg_add, show -C.canon = (-1 : ℤ) • C.canon by simp,
    show -Finsupp.single P (2 : ℤ) = Finsupp.single P (-2) by simp, deg_smul, deg_single,
    C.deg_canon] at h1
  omega

end CurveFFDer

/-- A curve function field with derivation, on which every `k`-automorphism permutes the points
and transforms the derivation by a multiplier, and with `h⁰(κ) ≥ g`. -/
private structure CurveFFAut (k K Pt : Type*) [Field k] [Field K] [Algebra k K]
    extends CurveFFDer k K Pt where
  perm : ∀ σ : K ≃ₐ[k] K, ∃ π : Pt → Pt, ∀ P (f : K), ord P (σ f) = ord (π P) f
  equiv : ∀ σ : K ≃ₐ[k] K, ∃ h : K, h ≠ 0 ∧ ∀ g : K, der (σ g) = h * σ (der g)
  rr_canon : (genus : ℤ) ≤ finrank k (toProperCurveFF.lin canon)

namespace CurveFFAut

variable (C : CurveFFAut k K Pt)

open ProperCurveFF CurveFFRR

/-- The permutation of the points induced by an automorphism. -/
private noncomputable def ptMap (σ : K ≃ₐ[k] K) : Pt → Pt := (C.perm σ).choose

private theorem isPointMap_ptMap (σ : K ≃ₐ[k] K) : C.IsPointMap σ (C.ptMap σ) :=
  (C.perm σ).choose_spec

private theorem ptMap_mul (σ τ : K ≃ₐ[k] K) : C.ptMap (σ * τ) = C.ptMap τ ∘ C.ptMap σ :=
  IsPointMap.unique _ (C.isPointMap_ptMap _) (IsPointMap.mul _ (C.isPointMap_ptMap σ)
    (C.isPointMap_ptMap τ))

private theorem ptMap_one : C.ptMap 1 = id :=
  IsPointMap.unique _ (C.isPointMap_ptMap _) (isPointMap_one _)

private theorem ptMap_inv_ptMap (σ : K ≃ₐ[k] K) (P : Pt) : C.ptMap σ⁻¹ (C.ptMap σ P) = P :=
  congrFun (IsPointMap.comp_inv _ (C.isPointMap_ptMap σ) (C.isPointMap_ptMap σ⁻¹)) P

private theorem ptMap_injective (σ : K ≃ₐ[k] K) : Function.Injective (C.ptMap σ) :=
  IsPointMap.injective _ (C.isPointMap_ptMap σ)

/-- The multiplier `h_σ` with `D (σ g) = h_σ σ (D g)`. -/
private noncomputable def mult (σ : K ≃ₐ[k] K) : K := (C.equiv σ).choose

private theorem mult_ne_zero (σ : K ≃ₐ[k] K) : C.mult σ ≠ 0 := (C.equiv σ).choose_spec.1

private theorem der_map (σ : K ≃ₐ[k] K) (g : K) : C.der (σ g) = C.mult σ * σ (C.der g) :=
  (C.equiv σ).choose_spec.2 g

private theorem exists_der_ne_zero : ∃ g : K, C.der g ≠ 0 := by
  obtain ⟨P⟩ := C.nonempty
  obtain ⟨t, -, hD, -⟩ := C.der_loc P
  exact ⟨t, hD⟩

private theorem mult_unique {σ : K ≃ₐ[k] K} {h : K} (hh : ∀ g, C.der (σ g) = h * σ (C.der g)) :
    C.mult σ = h := by
  obtain ⟨g, hg⟩ := C.exists_der_ne_zero
  have h1 := C.der_map σ g
  rw [hh g] at h1
  have : σ (C.der g) ≠ 0 := by simpa using hg
  exact (mul_right_cancel₀ this h1).symm

private theorem mult_mul (σ τ : K ≃ₐ[k] K) : C.mult (σ * τ) = C.mult σ * σ (C.mult τ) := by
  apply C.mult_unique
  intro g
  change C.der (σ (τ g)) = _ * σ (τ (C.der g))
  rw [C.der_map σ, C.der_map τ, map_mul]; ring

private theorem mult_one : C.mult 1 = 1 := C.mult_unique fun g => by simp

private theorem ord_mult [CharZero k] (σ : K ≃ₐ[k] K) (P : Pt) :
    C.ord P (C.mult σ) = C.canon (C.ptMap σ P) - C.canon P := by
  obtain ⟨t, ht, -, -, -⟩ := C.der_loc (C.ptMap σ P)
  have ht0 := C.ne_zero_of_ord_eq_one ht
  have hσt : C.ord P (σ t) = 1 := by rw [C.isPointMap_ptMap σ P, ht]
  have h1 := C.ord_der_of_ne_zero (f := σ t) (by simpa using ht0) (by rw [hσt]; omega)
  have h2 := C.ord_der_of_ne_zero (P := C.ptMap σ P) ht0 (by rw [ht]; omega)
  have e := C.der_map σ t
  have hσDt : σ (C.der t) ≠ 0 := by simpa using h2.1
  have h3 : C.ord P (C.der (σ t)) = C.ord P (C.mult σ) + C.ord P (σ (C.der t)) := by
    rw [e, C.ord_mul P _ _ (C.mult_ne_zero σ) hσDt]
  rw [h1.2, hσt, C.isPointMap_ptMap σ P, h2.2, ht] at h3
  omega

omit [Field K] [Algebra k K] in
private theorem add_le_deg_of_nonneg {E : Pt →₀ ℤ} (hE : ∀ Q, 0 ≤ E Q) {Q Q' : Pt} (h : Q ≠ Q') :
    E Q + E Q' ≤ deg E := by
  classical
  have hE' : ∀ R, 0 ≤ (E - Finsupp.single Q (E Q)) R := fun R => by
    simp only [Finsupp.sub_apply, Finsupp.single_apply]
    split_ifs with hR
    · subst hR; simp
    · simpa using hE R
  have h1 := le_deg_of_nonneg hE' Q'
  have h2 : deg (E - Finsupp.single Q (E Q)) = deg E - E Q := by
    rw [sub_eq_add_neg, deg_add, show -Finsupp.single Q (E Q) = Finsupp.single Q (-E Q) by simp,
      deg_single]; ring
  rw [h2] at h1
  simp only [Finsupp.sub_apply, Finsupp.single_apply, if_neg h, sub_zero] at h1
  linarith

omit [Field K] [Algebra k K] in
private theorem eq_zero_of_nonneg_of_deg_eq_zero {E : Pt →₀ ℤ} (hE : ∀ Q, 0 ≤ E Q) (h : deg E = 0)
    (Q : Pt) : E Q = 0 := le_antisymm (h ▸ le_deg_of_nonneg hE Q) (hE Q)

/-- A function whose divisor is `P₁ - P₂`, in genus zero. -/
private theorem exists_div_eq_sub [CharZero k] (hg : C.genus = 0) {P₁ P₂ : Pt} (h12 : P₁ ≠ P₂) :
    ∃ f : K, f ≠ 0 ∧ C.ord P₁ f = 1 ∧ C.ord P₂ f = -1 ∧ ∀ Q, Q ≠ P₁ → Q ≠ P₂ → C.ord Q f = 0 := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨f, hf0, hfg, hfP, hfQ⟩ := C.exists_pole_only_at P₂
  rw [hg] at hfg
  have hP2 : C.ord P₂ f = -1 := by push_cast at hfg; omega
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := C.residue P₁ f (hfQ P₁ h12)
  rcases hc with hc | hc
  · exfalso; rw [hc, C.ord_algebraMap P₂] at hP2
    · omega
    · rintro rfl; rw [map_zero] at hc; exact hf0 hc
  set g := f - algebraMap k K c
  have hg0 : g ≠ 0 := fun h => by rw [h, C.ord_zero] at hc; omega
  have hgP2 : C.ord P₂ g = -1 := by
    rw [C.ord_sub_algebraMap_of_neg P₂ hf0 (by omega), hP2]
  have hgQ : ∀ Q, Q ≠ P₂ → 0 ≤ C.ord Q g := fun Q hQ =>
    C.ord_sub_algebraMap_nonneg Q (hfQ Q hQ) hg0
  set E : Pt →₀ ℤ := C.div g hg0 + Finsupp.single P₂ 1
  have hEapp : ∀ Q, E Q = C.ord Q g + if P₂ = Q then 1 else 0 := fun Q => by
    simp [E, Finsupp.single_apply]
  have hE : ∀ Q, 0 ≤ E Q := fun Q => by
    rw [hEapp]
    by_cases hQ : P₂ = Q
    · subst hQ; rw [if_pos rfl, hgP2]; omega
    · rw [if_neg hQ]; have := hgQ Q (Ne.symm hQ); omega
  have hdeg : deg E = 1 := by
    rw [deg_add, C.deg_div_eq_zero, deg_single, zero_add]
  have hE1 : E P₁ = 1 := by
    have := le_deg_of_nonneg hE P₁
    rw [hEapp, if_neg (Ne.symm h12)] at this ⊢
    omega
  refine ⟨g, hg0, by have := hEapp P₁; rw [if_neg (Ne.symm h12)] at this; omega, hgP2,
    fun Q hQ1 hQ2 => ?_⟩
  have := add_le_deg_of_nonneg hE (Ne.symm hQ1)
  rw [hE1, hdeg, hEapp, if_neg (Ne.symm hQ2)] at this
  have := hgQ Q hQ2
  omega

private theorem der_algebraMap_mul (c : k) (x : K) :
    C.der (algebraMap k K c * x) = algebraMap k K c * C.der x := by
  rw [← Algebra.smul_def, C.der.map_smul, Algebra.smul_def]

/-- The functions whose orders all vanish are the nonzero constants, up to `0`. -/
private theorem exists_eq_mul_of_ord_eq {f g : K} (hg : g ≠ 0)
    (h : ∀ Q, C.ord Q g ≤ C.ord Q f ∨ f = 0) :
    ∃ c : k, f = algebraMap k K c * g := by
  by_cases hf : f = 0
  · exact ⟨0, by rw [hf, map_zero, zero_mul]⟩
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := C.const (f / g) fun Q => by
    rw [C.ord_div Q hf hg]
    rcases h Q with h | h
    · omega
    · exact absurd h hf
  exact ⟨c, by rw [← hc]; field_simp⟩

/-- **The two-point case in genus zero.** On a curve of genus zero with two marked points, every
automorphism preserving the pair acts on the one-dimensional `L(m (κ + P₁ + P₂))`, twisted by
the `m`-th power of its multiplier, as `1` or `(-1)^m`. -/
private theorem twoPoint_action [CharZero k] (hg : C.genus = 0) {P₁ P₂ : Pt} (h12 : P₁ ≠ P₂) (m : ℕ)
    (σ : K ≃ₐ[k] K)
    (hσ : ∀ Q, (C.ptMap σ Q = P₁ ∨ C.ptMap σ Q = P₂) ↔ (Q = P₁ ∨ Q = P₂)) :
    ∃ ε : k, (ε = 1 ∨ ε = (-1) ^ m) ∧
      ∀ f ∈ C.lin ((m : ℤ) • C.canon + (m : ℤ) • (Finsupp.single P₁ 1 + Finsupp.single P₂ 1)),
        σ f * C.mult σ ^ m = algebraMap k K ε * f := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨f', hf'0, hf1, hf2, hfQ⟩ := C.exists_div_eq_sub hg h12
  set Bd : Pt →₀ ℤ := Finsupp.single P₁ 1 + Finsupp.single P₂ 1
  have hBd : ∀ Q, Bd Q = if Q = P₁ ∨ Q = P₂ then 1 else 0 := fun Q => by
    simp only [Bd, Finsupp.add_apply, Finsupp.single_apply]
    by_cases h1 : Q = P₁
    · subst h1; simp [h12, Ne.symm h12]
    · by_cases h2 : Q = P₂
      · subst h2; simp [h12, Ne.symm h12]
      · simp [h1, h2, Ne.symm h1, Ne.symm h2]
  have hD1 := C.ord_der_of_ne_zero (P := P₁) hf'0 (by rw [hf1]; omega)
  have hD0 : C.der f' ≠ 0 := hD1.1
  set u := C.der f' / f'
  have hu0 : u ≠ 0 := div_ne_zero hD0 hf'0
  have hu : ∀ Q, C.ord Q u + C.canon Q + Bd Q = 0 := by
    have hge : ∀ Q, 0 ≤ (C.div u hu0 + C.canon + Bd) Q := fun Q => by
      simp only [Finsupp.add_apply, div_apply, hBd]
      simp only [u]; rw [C.ord_div Q hD0 hf'0]
      by_cases h1 : Q = P₁
      · subst h1; rw [if_pos (Or.inl rfl), hD1.2, hf1]; omega
      by_cases h2 : Q = P₂
      · subst h2
        have hD2 := C.ord_der_of_ne_zero (P := Q) hf'0 (by rw [hf2]; omega)
        rw [if_pos (Or.inr rfl), hD2.2, hf2]; omega
      rw [if_neg (by tauto), hfQ Q h1 h2]
      rcases C.der_eq_zero_or_le (P := Q) (f := f') (Or.inr (by rw [hfQ Q h1 h2])) with h | h
      · exact absurd h hD0
      · omega
    have hdeg : deg (C.div u hu0 + C.canon + Bd) = 0 := by
      rw [deg_add, deg_add, C.deg_div_eq_zero, C.deg_canon, hg]
      simp only [Bd, deg_add, deg_single]; push_cast
    intro Q
    have := eq_zero_of_nonneg_of_deg_eq_zero hge hdeg Q
    simpa using this
  -- the linear system is spanned by `u ^ m`
  have hspan : ∀ f ∈ C.lin ((m : ℤ) • C.canon + (m : ℤ) • Bd),
      ∃ c : k, f = algebraMap k K c * u ^ m := by
    intro f hf
    refine C.exists_eq_mul_of_ord_eq (pow_ne_zero _ hu0) fun Q => ?_
    rcases hf with hf | hf
    · exact Or.inr hf
    · left
      have := hf Q
      have h2 := hu Q
      simp only [Finsupp.add_apply, Finsupp.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul] at this
      rw [C.ord_pow Q hu0]
      nlinarith
  -- the action of `σ` on `u`
  have hσP : C.ptMap σ P₁ = P₁ ∨ C.ptMap σ P₁ = P₂ := (hσ P₁).mpr (Or.inl rfl)
  have hσu : σ u * C.mult σ = u ∨ σ u * C.mult σ = -u := by
    have hπ := C.isPointMap_ptMap σ
    have hinj := C.ptMap_injective σ
    have hother : ∀ Q, Q ≠ P₁ → Q ≠ P₂ → C.ptMap σ Q ≠ P₁ ∧ C.ptMap σ Q ≠ P₂ := fun Q h1 h2 => by
      have := (hσ Q).not.mpr (by tauto)
      tauto
    have hσf0 : σ f' ≠ 0 := by simpa using hf'0
    have hmult := C.mult_ne_zero σ
    have hσD : C.der (σ f') = C.mult σ * σ (C.der f') := C.der_map σ f'
    rcases hσP with h1 | h1
    · have h2 : C.ptMap σ P₂ = P₂ := by
        rcases (hσ P₂).mpr (Or.inr rfl) with h | h
        · exact absurd (hinj (h.trans h1.symm)) (Ne.symm h12)
        · exact h
      have hord : ∀ Q, C.ord Q (σ f') = C.ord Q f' := fun Q => by
        rw [hπ Q]
        by_cases hQ1 : Q = P₁
        · subst hQ1; rw [h1]
        by_cases hQ2 : Q = P₂
        · subst hQ2; rw [h2]
        obtain ⟨h3, h4⟩ := hother Q hQ1 hQ2
        rw [hfQ _ h3 h4, hfQ Q hQ1 hQ2]
      obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := C.exists_eq_mul_of_ord_eq (f := σ f') hf'0 fun Q => Or.inl (hord Q).ge
      have ha0 : algebraMap k K a ≠ 0 := fun h0 => hσf0 (by rw [ha, h0, zero_mul])
      left
      have e1 : σ (C.der f') = algebraMap k K a * C.der f' / C.mult σ := by
        rw [eq_div_iff hmult, mul_comm, ← hσD, ha, C.der_algebraMap_mul]
      simp only [u, map_div₀, e1, ha]
      field_simp
    · have h2 : C.ptMap σ P₂ = P₁ := by
        rcases (hσ P₂).mpr (Or.inr rfl) with h | h
        · exact h
        · exact absurd (hinj (h.trans h1.symm)) (Ne.symm h12)
      have hord : ∀ Q, C.ord Q (σ f') = C.ord Q f'⁻¹ := fun Q => by
        rw [hπ Q, C.ord_inv Q hf'0]
        by_cases hQ1 : Q = P₁
        · subst hQ1; rw [h1, hf1, hf2]
        by_cases hQ2 : Q = P₂
        · subst hQ2; rw [h2, hf1, hf2]; rfl
        obtain ⟨h3, h4⟩ := hother Q hQ1 hQ2
        rw [hfQ _ h3 h4, hfQ Q hQ1 hQ2]; rfl
      obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := C.exists_eq_mul_of_ord_eq (f := σ f') (inv_ne_zero hf'0)
        fun Q => Or.inl (hord Q).ge
      have ha0 : algebraMap k K a ≠ 0 := fun h0 => hσf0 (by rw [ha, h0, zero_mul])
      right
      have e1 : σ (C.der f') = algebraMap k K a * (-(f'⁻¹) ^ 2 * C.der f') / C.mult σ := by
        rw [eq_div_iff hmult, mul_comm, ← hσD, ha, C.der_algebraMap_mul, Derivation.leibniz_inv,
          smul_eq_mul]
      simp only [u, map_div₀, e1, ha]
      field_simp
  obtain ⟨ε, hε, hεu⟩ : ∃ ε : k, (ε = 1 ∨ ε = (-1) ^ m) ∧ (σ u * C.mult σ) ^ m =
      algebraMap k K ε * u ^ m := by
    rcases hσu with h | h
    · exact ⟨1, Or.inl rfl, by rw [h, map_one, one_mul]⟩
    · exact ⟨(-1) ^ m, Or.inr rfl, by rw [h, map_pow, map_neg, map_one, neg_pow]⟩
  refine ⟨ε, hε, fun f hf => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨c, rfl⟩ := hspan f hf
  rw [map_mul, map_pow, AlgEquiv.commutes, mul_assoc, ← mul_pow, hεu]
  ring

/-- The stabilizer of a point. -/
private def stab (O : Pt) : Subgroup (K ≃ₐ[k] K) where
  carrier := {σ | C.ptMap σ O = O}
  one_mem' := by simp [C.ptMap_one]
  mul_mem' := fun {σ τ} hσ hτ => by
    simp only [Set.mem_setOf_eq] at *; rw [C.ptMap_mul]; simp [hσ, hτ]
  inv_mem' := fun {σ} hσ => by
    simp only [Set.mem_setOf_eq] at *
    conv_lhs => rw [← hσ]
    exact C.ptMap_inv_ptMap σ O

/-- In genus `g ≥ 1` the stabilizer of a point is finite. -/
private theorem finite_stab [CharZero k] (hg : 1 ≤ C.genus) (O : Pt) :
    (C.stab O : Set (K ≃ₐ[k] K)).Finite := by
  classical
  refine C.finite_of_twist hg (Dv := ((3 * C.genus + 2 : ℕ) : ℤ) • Finsupp.single O 1) ?_ _
    C.ptMap (fun σ => C.ptMap σ⁻¹) fun σ hσ => ⟨C.isPointMap_ptMap σ, C.isPointMap_ptMap σ⁻¹,
      1, one_ne_zero, fun P => ?_⟩
  · rw [deg_smul, deg_single]; push_cast; omega
  · change C.ptMap σ O = O at hσ
    rw [C.ord_one, zero_add]
    simp only [Finsupp.smul_apply, Finsupp.single_apply, smul_eq_mul]
    congr 1
    by_cases hP : O = P
    · subst hP; simp [hσ]
    · rw [if_neg hP, if_neg]
      intro h; apply hP
      exact C.ptMap_injective σ (hσ.trans h)

private theorem pow_card_stab_eq_one [CharZero k] (hg : 1 ≤ C.genus) (O : Pt) {σ : K ≃ₐ[k] K}
    (hσ : σ ∈ C.stab O) : σ ^ Nat.card (C.stab O) = 1 := by
  haveI : Finite (C.stab O) := (C.finite_stab hg O).to_subtype
  have := pow_card_eq_one' (G := C.stab O) (x := ⟨σ, hσ⟩)
  exact congrArg Subtype.val this

/-- **Genus one, no boundary.** The automorphisms act on the one-dimensional `L(m κ)`, twisted by
the `m`-th power of their multipliers, through finitely many scalars. -/
private theorem genusOne_finite_scalars [CharZero k] (hg : C.genus = 1) (m : ℕ)
    (hinv : ∀ O O' : Pt, O ≠ O' → ∃ ρ : K ≃ₐ[k] K, ρ * ρ = 1 ∧ C.ptMap ρ O' = O) :
    ∃ S : Set k, S.Finite ∧ ∀ σ : K ≃ₐ[k] K, ∃ ε ∈ S,
      ∀ f ∈ C.lin ((m : ℤ) • C.canon), σ f * C.mult σ ^ m = algebraMap k K ε * f := by
  classical
  have hrr := C.rr_canon
  rw [hg] at hrr
  obtain ⟨c0, hc0, hc00⟩ := Submodule.exists_mem_ne_zero_of_ne_bot (p := C.lin C.canon) (by
    intro h; rw [h, finrank_bot] at hrr; omega)
  have hc0ord : ∀ P, C.ord P c0 = -C.canon P := by
    have hE : ∀ P, 0 ≤ (C.div c0 hc00 + C.canon) P := fun P => by
      rcases hc0 with h | h
      · exact absurd h hc00
      · simpa using h P
    have hd : deg (C.div c0 hc00 + C.canon) = 0 := by
      rw [deg_add, C.deg_div_eq_zero, C.deg_canon, hg]; ring
    intro P
    have := eq_zero_of_nonneg_of_deg_eq_zero hE hd P
    simp at this; omega
  -- the scalar `ψ σ`
  have hψ : ∀ σ : K ≃ₐ[k] K, ∃ c : k, σ c0 * C.mult σ / c0 = algebraMap k K c := fun σ =>
    C.const _ fun P => by
      have h0 : σ c0 ≠ 0 := by simpa using hc00
      rw [C.ord_div P (mul_ne_zero h0 (C.mult_ne_zero σ)) hc00,
        C.ord_mul P _ _ h0 (C.mult_ne_zero σ), C.isPointMap_ptMap σ P, hc0ord, hc0ord,
        C.ord_mult]
      omega
  choose ψ hψeq using hψ
  have hψ' : ∀ σ, σ c0 * C.mult σ = algebraMap k K (ψ σ) * c0 := fun σ => by
    rw [← hψeq σ]; field_simp
  have hψmul : ∀ σ τ, ψ (σ * τ) = ψ σ * ψ τ := fun σ τ => by
    apply (algebraMap k K).injective
    have e := hψ' (σ * τ)
    rw [C.mult_mul] at e
    change σ (τ c0) * (C.mult σ * σ (C.mult τ)) = _ at e
    have e2 : σ (τ c0) * (C.mult σ * σ (C.mult τ)) = σ (τ c0 * C.mult τ) * C.mult σ := by
      rw [map_mul]; ring
    rw [e2, hψ' τ, map_mul, AlgEquiv.commutes, mul_assoc, hψ' σ] at e
    rw [map_mul]
    exact mul_right_cancel₀ hc00 (by rw [← e]; ring)
  have hψone : ψ 1 = 1 := by
    apply (algebraMap k K).injective
    have e := hψ' 1
    rw [C.mult_one] at e
    rw [map_one]
    exact mul_right_cancel₀ hc00 (by rw [← e]; simp)
  have hψpow : ∀ σ (n : ℕ), ψ (σ ^ n) = ψ σ ^ n := fun σ n => by
    induction n with
    | zero => simp [hψone]
    | succ n ih => rw [pow_succ, hψmul, ih, pow_succ]
  obtain ⟨O⟩ := C.nonempty
  set n := Nat.card (C.stab O)
  have hg1 : 1 ≤ C.genus := by omega
  have hn : ∀ σ ∈ C.stab O, ψ σ ^ n = 1 := fun σ hσ => by
    rw [← hψpow, C.pow_card_stab_eq_one hg1 O hσ, hψone]
  have hall : ∀ σ, ψ σ ^ (2 * n) = 1 := by
    intro σ
    by_cases hO : C.ptMap σ O = O
    · rw [pow_mul', hn σ hO, one_pow]
    · obtain ⟨ρ, hρ, hρO⟩ := hinv O (C.ptMap σ O) (Ne.symm hO)
      have hσρ : σ * ρ ∈ C.stab O := by
        change C.ptMap (σ * ρ) O = O
        rw [C.ptMap_mul]; exact hρO
      have h1 := hn _ hσρ
      have h2 : ψ ρ * ψ ρ = 1 := by rw [← hψmul, hρ, hψone]
      rw [hψmul] at h1
      have : (ψ σ * ψ ρ) ^ n * (ψ σ * ψ ρ) ^ n = ψ σ ^ (2 * n) * (ψ ρ * ψ ρ) ^ n := by ring
      rw [h1, one_mul, h2, one_pow, mul_one] at this
      exact this.symm
  have hnpos : 0 < n := by
    haveI : Finite (C.stab O) := (C.finite_stab hg1 O).to_subtype
    exact Nat.card_pos
  refine ⟨(fun x => x ^ m) '' {x : k | x ^ (2 * n) = 1}, ?_, fun σ => ⟨ψ σ ^ m,
    ⟨ψ σ, hall σ, rfl⟩, fun f hf => ?_⟩⟩
  · refine Set.Finite.image _ ?_
    have hp : (Polynomial.X ^ (2 * n) - 1 : Polynomial k) ≠ 0 :=
      Polynomial.X_pow_sub_C_ne_zero (by omega) 1
    refine ((Polynomial.X ^ (2 * n) - 1 : Polynomial k).roots.toFinset.finite_toSet).subset ?_
    intro x hx
    simp only [Set.mem_setOf_eq] at hx
    simp [Polynomial.mem_roots hp, hx]
  · obtain ⟨c, rfl⟩ := C.exists_eq_mul_of_ord_eq (pow_ne_zero m hc00) (f := f) fun Q => by
      rcases hf with hf | hf
      · exact Or.inr hf
      · left
        have := hf Q
        simp only [Finsupp.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul] at this
        rw [C.ord_pow Q hc00, hc0ord]; linarith
    rw [map_mul, map_pow, AlgEquiv.commutes, mul_assoc, ← mul_pow, hψ', mul_pow, map_pow]
    ring

end CurveFFAut

namespace CurveFFRR

variable (C : CurveFFRR k K Pt)

/-- An automorphism fixing a point and a uniformizer there is the identity. -/
private theorem eq_one_of_fixes_uniformizer {σ : K ≃ₐ[k] K} {π : Pt → Pt} (hπ : C.IsPointMap σ π)
    {P : Pt} (hP : π P = P) {t : K} (ht : C.ord P t = 1) (hσt : σ t = t) : σ = 1 := by
  have ht0 := C.ne_zero_of_ord_eq_one ht
  have hσO : ∀ g ∈ C.valRing P, σ g ∈ C.valRing P := fun g hg => by
    rcases hg with h | h
    · left; rw [h, map_zero]
    · right; rw [hπ P, hP]; exact h
  have key : ∀ n : ℕ, ∀ g ∈ C.valRing P, σ g - g = 0 ∨ (n : ℤ) ≤ C.ord P (σ g - g) := by
    intro n
    induction n with
    | zero =>
      intro g hg
      have := (C.valRing P).sub_mem (hσO g hg) hg
      rcases this with h | h
      · exact Or.inl h
      · exact Or.inr (by simpa using h)
    | succ n ih =>
      intro g hg
      obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := C.exists_isRes hg
      rcases hc with hc | hc
      · left
        have : g = algebraMap k K c := by linear_combination hc
        rw [this, AlgEquiv.commutes, sub_self]
      set g₁ := (g - algebraMap k K c) / t
      have hg₁ : g₁ ∈ C.valRing P := by
        by_cases h0 : g - algebraMap k K c = 0
        · left; simp [g₁, h0]
        · right; simp only [g₁]; rw [C.ord_div P h0 ht0, ht]; omega
      have hgg : g = algebraMap k K c + t * g₁ := by simp only [g₁]; field_simp; ring
      have e : σ g - g = t * (σ g₁ - g₁) := by
        conv_lhs => rw [hgg]
        rw [map_add, map_mul, AlgEquiv.commutes, hσt]; ring
      rcases ih g₁ hg₁ with h | h
      · left; rw [e, h, mul_zero]
      · by_cases h0 : σ g₁ - g₁ = 0
        · left; rw [e, h0, mul_zero]
        · right; rw [e, C.ord_mul P _ _ ht0 h0, ht]; push_cast; omega
  have hfixO : ∀ g ∈ C.valRing P, σ g = g := fun g hg => by
    by_contra hne
    have h0 : σ g - g ≠ 0 := sub_ne_zero.mpr hne
    rcases key ((C.ord P (σ g - g)).toNat + 1) g hg with h | h
    · exact h0 h
    · have := Int.self_le_toNat (C.ord P (σ g - g)); push_cast at h; omega
  ext g
  by_cases hg : g = 0
  · rw [hg, map_zero]; rfl
  set N := (-C.ord P g).toNat
  have htN : t ^ N ∈ C.valRing P := Or.inr (by rw [C.ord_pow P ht0, ht]; omega)
  have hgt : g * t ^ N ∈ C.valRing P := Or.inr (by
    rw [C.ord_mul P _ _ hg (pow_ne_zero _ ht0), C.ord_pow P ht0, ht]
    have := Int.self_le_toNat (-C.ord P g); omega)
  have e1 := hfixO _ hgt
  have e2 := hfixO _ htN
  rw [map_mul, e2] at e1
  exact mul_right_cancel₀ (pow_ne_zero _ ht0) e1

end CurveFFRR

namespace CurveFF

open Polynomial in
/-- A polynomial in a function with a simple pole at `R` has a pole of order its degree. -/
private theorem ord_aeval {R : Pt} {x : K} (hx : C.ord R x = -1) {p : k[X]} (hp : p ≠ 0) :
    aeval x p ≠ 0 ∧ C.ord R (aeval x p) = -p.natDegree := by
  classical
  have hx0 : x ≠ 0 := fun h => by rw [h, C.ord_zero] at hx; omega
  have hsum : aeval x p = ∑ i ∈ p.support, algebraMap k K (p.coeff i) * x ^ i := by
    rw [aeval_def, eval₂_eq_sum, Polynomial.sum_def]
  have hterm : ∀ i ∈ p.support, algebraMap k K (p.coeff i) * x ^ i ≠ 0 := fun i hi =>
    mul_ne_zero (by simpa using mem_support_iff.mp hi) (pow_ne_zero _ hx0)
  have hord : ∀ i ∈ p.support, C.ord R (algebraMap k K (p.coeff i) * x ^ i) = -i := fun i hi => by
    rw [C.ord_mul R _ _ (by simpa using mem_support_iff.mp hi) (pow_ne_zero _ hx0),
      C.ord_algebraMap R _ (mem_support_iff.mp hi), C.ord_pow R hx0, hx]; ring
  obtain ⟨i, hi, hne, hordi, hmin⟩ := C.ord_sum_of_injOn R p.support
    (nonempty_support_iff.mpr hp) _ hterm (fun a ha b hb hab => by
      have := hord a ha; have := hord b hb; simp only at hab; omega)
  rw [hsum]
  refine ⟨hne, ?_⟩
  rw [hordi, hord i hi]
  have h1 : i ≤ p.natDegree := le_natDegree_of_mem_supp i hi
  have h2 := hmin p.natDegree (natDegree_mem_support_of_nonzero hp)
  rw [hord i hi, hord _ (natDegree_mem_support_of_nonzero hp)] at h2
  omega

open Polynomial in
/-- A function with simple poles at `O` and `O'`: every element of `k(x)` has the same order at
`O` and `O'`. -/
private theorem ord_eq_of_mem_adjoin {O O' : Pt} {x : K} (hO : C.ord O x = -1)
    (hO' : C.ord O' x = -1)
    {y : K} (hy : y ∈ IntermediateField.adjoin k {x}) (hy0 : y ≠ 0) : C.ord O y = C.ord O' y := by
  obtain ⟨r, s, rfl⟩ := (IntermediateField.mem_adjoin_simple_iff (F := k) y).mp hy
  have hs : aeval x s ≠ 0 := fun h => hy0 (by rw [h, div_zero])
  have hr : aeval x r ≠ 0 := fun h => hy0 (by rw [h, zero_div])
  have hr0 : r ≠ 0 := fun h => hr (by rw [h, map_zero])
  have hs0 : s ≠ 0 := fun h => hs (by rw [h, map_zero])
  rw [C.ord_div O hr hs, C.ord_div O' hr hs, (C.ord_aeval hO hr0).2, (C.ord_aeval hO hs0).2,
    (C.ord_aeval hO' hr0).2, (C.ord_aeval hO' hs0).2]

end CurveFF

namespace ProperCurveFF

variable (C : ProperCurveFF k K Pt)

open Polynomial in
/-- **Clearing poles.** If `x` has no pole outside `{O, O'}`, every nonzero `y` becomes regular
outside `{O, O'}` after multiplication by a nonzero polynomial in `x`. -/
private theorem exists_aeval_mul_nonneg {O O' : Pt} {x : K}
    (hx : ∀ Q, Q ≠ O → Q ≠ O' → 0 ≤ C.ord Q x) (hxc : ∀ c : k, x ≠ algebraMap k K c)
    {y : K} (hy : y ≠ 0) :
    ∃ p : k[X], p ≠ 0 ∧ ∀ Q, Q ≠ O → Q ≠ O' → 0 ≤ C.ord Q (aeval x p * y) := by
  classical
  have hfin := C.finite_support y hy
  set S := hfin.toFinset.filter fun Q => Q ≠ O ∧ Q ≠ O'
  have hres : ∀ Q ∈ S, ∃ c : k, C.IsRes Q x c := fun Q hQ => by
    obtain ⟨-, h1, h2⟩ := Finset.mem_filter.mp hQ
    exact C.exists_isRes (Or.inr (hx Q h1 h2))
  choose! c hc using hres
  set n : Pt → ℕ := fun Q => (-C.ord Q y).toNat
  set p : k[X] := ∏ Q ∈ S, (Polynomial.X - Polynomial.C (c Q)) ^ n Q
  have hfac : ∀ Q, x - algebraMap k K (c Q) ≠ 0 := fun Q h => hxc (c Q) (by linear_combination h)
  refine ⟨p, Finset.prod_ne_zero_iff.mpr fun Q _ => pow_ne_zero _ (X_sub_C_ne_zero _),
    fun Q hQO hQO' => ?_⟩
  have hev : aeval x p = ∏ Q' ∈ S, (x - algebraMap k K (c Q')) ^ n Q' := by
    simp [p, map_prod]
  have hp0 : aeval x p ≠ 0 := by
    rw [hev]; exact Finset.prod_ne_zero_iff.mpr fun Q' _ => pow_ne_zero _ (hfac Q')
  have hordp : C.ord Q (aeval x p) =
      ∑ Q' ∈ S, (n Q' : ℤ) * C.ord Q (x - algebraMap k K (c Q')) := by
    rw [hev, C.ord_prod Q _ _ fun Q' _ => pow_ne_zero _ (hfac Q')]
    exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun Q' _ => C.ord_pow Q (hfac Q') _
  have hfac_nonneg : ∀ Q', 0 ≤ C.ord Q (x - algebraMap k K (c Q')) := fun Q' =>
    C.ord_sub_algebraMap_nonneg Q (hx Q hQO hQO') (hfac Q')
  rw [C.ord_mul Q _ _ hp0 hy, hordp]
  by_cases hQS : Q ∈ S
  · have hsplit := Finset.add_sum_erase S
      (fun Q' => (n Q' : ℤ) * C.ord Q (x - algebraMap k K (c Q'))) hQS
    have hrest : 0 ≤ ∑ Q' ∈ S.erase Q, (n Q' : ℤ) * C.ord Q (x - algebraMap k K (c Q')) :=
      Finset.sum_nonneg fun Q' _ => mul_nonneg (by positivity) (hfac_nonneg Q')
    have hQ1 : 1 ≤ C.ord Q (x - algebraMap k K (c Q)) := by
      rcases hc Q hQS with h | h
      · exact absurd h (hfac Q)
      · exact h
    have hn : -C.ord Q y ≤ (n Q : ℤ) := Int.self_le_toNat _
    have hn0 : (0 : ℤ) ≤ n Q := by positivity
    rw [← hsplit]
    nlinarith
  · have hy0 : 0 ≤ C.ord Q y := by
      by_contra hneg
      apply hQS
      refine Finset.mem_filter.mpr ⟨?_, hQO, hQO'⟩
      simp only [Set.Finite.mem_toFinset, Function.mem_support]; omega
    have : 0 ≤ ∑ Q' ∈ S, (n Q' : ℤ) * C.ord Q (x - algebraMap k K (c Q')) :=
      Finset.sum_nonneg fun Q' _ => mul_nonneg (by positivity) (hfac_nonneg Q')
    omega

open Polynomial in
private theorem aeval_mem_adjoin (x : K) (q : k[X]) : aeval x q ∈ IntermediateField.adjoin k {x} :=
  (IntermediateField.mem_adjoin_simple_iff (F := k) _).mpr ⟨q, 1, by simp⟩

open Polynomial in
/-- **The degree of a function with two simple poles.** If `x` has simple poles at `O ≠ O'` and
no other pole, then `K` has dimension at most two over `k(x)`. -/
private theorem finrank_adjoin_le_two {O O' : Pt} (hOO' : O ≠ O') {x : K} (hO : C.ord O x = -1)
    (hO' : C.ord O' x = -1) (hx : ∀ Q, Q ≠ O → Q ≠ O' → 0 ≤ C.ord Q x) :
    FiniteDimensional (IntermediateField.adjoin k {x}) K ∧
      finrank (IntermediateField.adjoin k {x}) K ≤ 2 := by
  classical
  set F := IntermediateField.adjoin k {x}
  have hxc : ∀ c : k, x ≠ algebraMap k K c := fun c h => by
    by_cases hc : c = 0
    · rw [h, hc, map_zero, C.ord_zero] at hO; omega
    · rw [h, C.ord_algebraMap O c hc] at hO; omega
  have hx0 : x ≠ 0 := fun h => by rw [h, C.ord_zero] at hO; omega
  have key : ∀ s : Finset K, LinearIndependent F (fun i : s => (i : K)) → s.card ≤ 2 := by
    intro s hs
    by_contra hd
    push Not at hd
    have hy0 : ∀ y : s, (y : K) ≠ 0 := hs.ne_zero
    have hp := fun y : s => C.exists_aeval_mul_nonneg hx hxc (hy0 y)
    choose p hp0 hpQ using hp
    set y' : s → K := fun y => aeval x (p y) * y
    have hy'0 : ∀ y, y' y ≠ 0 := fun y =>
      mul_ne_zero (C.ord_aeval hO (hp0 y)).1 (hy0 y)
    set M : ℕ := Finset.univ.sup fun y : s =>
      (-(min (C.ord O (y' y)) (C.ord O' (y' y)))).toNat
    have hM : ∀ y, -(M : ℤ) ≤ C.ord O (y' y) ∧ -(M : ℤ) ≤ C.ord O' (y' y) := fun y => by
      have h1 : (-(min (C.ord O (y' y)) (C.ord O' (y' y)))).toNat ≤ M :=
        Finset.le_sup (f := fun y : s => (-(min (C.ord O (y' y)) (C.ord O' (y' y)))).toNat)
          (Finset.mem_univ y)
      have h2 := Int.self_le_toNat (-(min (C.ord O (y' y)) (C.ord O' (y' y))))
      have h3 : ((-(min (C.ord O (y' y)) (C.ord O' (y' y)))).toNat : ℤ) ≤ M := by exact_mod_cast h1
      constructor <;> [have := min_le_left (C.ord O (y' y)) (C.ord O' (y' y));
        have := min_le_right (C.ord O (y' y)) (C.ord O' (y' y))] <;> omega
    set n : ℕ := 2 * M
    set Dv : Pt →₀ ℤ := ((n + M : ℕ) : ℤ) • (Finsupp.single O 1 + Finsupp.single O' 1)
    have hDv : ∀ Q, Dv Q = if Q = O ∨ Q = O' then ((n + M : ℕ) : ℤ) else 0 := fun Q => by
      simp only [Dv, Finsupp.smul_apply, Finsupp.add_apply, Finsupp.single_apply, smul_eq_mul]
      by_cases h1 : Q = O
      · subst h1; simp [hOO', Ne.symm hOO']
      · by_cases h2 : Q = O'
        · subst h2; simp [hOO', Ne.symm hOO']
        · simp [h1, h2, Ne.symm h1, Ne.symm h2]
    set Φ : s × Fin (n + 1) → K := fun i => x ^ (i.2 : ℕ) * y' i.1
    have hΦmem : ∀ i, Φ i ∈ C.lin Dv := fun i => by
      right; intro Q
      have hne : x ^ (i.2 : ℕ) ≠ 0 := pow_ne_zero _ hx0
      simp only [Φ]
      rw [C.ord_mul Q _ _ hne (hy'0 _), C.ord_pow Q hx0, hDv]
      have hj : ((i.2 : ℕ) : ℤ) ≤ n := by have := i.2.2; omega
      by_cases h1 : Q = O
      · subst h1; rw [if_pos (Or.inl rfl), hO]; have := (hM i.1).1; push_cast at *; nlinarith
      by_cases h2 : Q = O'
      · subst h2; rw [if_pos (Or.inr rfl), hO']; have := (hM i.1).2; push_cast at *; nlinarith
      rw [if_neg (by tauto)]
      have := hpQ i.1 Q h1 h2
      have := hx Q h1 h2
      simp only [y'] at *
      nlinarith
    have hli : LinearIndependent k (fun i => (⟨Φ i, hΦmem i⟩ : C.lin Dv)) := by
      apply LinearIndependent.of_comp (C.lin Dv).subtype
      rw [Fintype.linearIndependent_iff]
      intro g hg
      simp only [Function.comp_apply, Submodule.subtype_apply] at hg
      set q : s → k[X] := fun y =>
        ∑ j : Fin (n + 1), Polynomial.C (g (y, j)) * Polynomial.X ^ (j : ℕ)
      have hterm : ∀ y : s, (⟨aeval x (q y * p y), aeval_mem_adjoin (k := k) x _⟩ : F) • (y : K) =
          ∑ j : Fin (n + 1), g (y, j) • Φ (y, j) := by
        intro y
        change aeval x (q y * p y) * (y : K) = _
        simp only [q, Φ, y', map_mul, map_sum, aeval_C, aeval_X, map_pow, Algebra.smul_def,
          Finset.sum_mul]
        exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun j _ => by ring
      have hsum : ∑ y : s, (⟨aeval x (q y * p y), aeval_mem_adjoin (k := k) x _⟩ : F) • (y : K) =
          0 := by
        rw [Finset.sum_congr rfl fun y _ => hterm y]
        rw [Fintype.sum_prod_type] at hg
        exact hg
      have h1 := (Fintype.linearIndependent_iff.mp hs) _ hsum
      intro ⟨y, j⟩
      have h2 : aeval x (q y * p y) = 0 := congrArg Subtype.val (h1 y)
      have h3 : q y * p y = 0 := by
        by_contra hne; exact (C.ord_aeval hO hne).1 h2
      have h4 : q y = 0 := (mul_eq_zero.mp h3).resolve_right (hp0 y)
      have h5 := congrArg (fun r => Polynomial.coeff r (j : ℕ)) h4
      simp only [q, Polynomial.finset_sum_coeff, Polynomial.coeff_C_mul_X_pow,
        Polynomial.coeff_zero] at h5
      rw [Finset.sum_eq_single j (fun j' _ hj' => by
        rw [if_neg]; intro h; exact hj' (Fin.ext h.symm)) (by simp)] at h5
      simpa using h5
    have hcard := hli.fintype_card_le_finrank
    have hdim := C.finrank_lin_le Dv
    have hdeg : deg Dv = 2 * ((n + M : ℕ) : ℤ) := by
      simp only [Dv, deg_smul, deg_add, deg_single]; ring
    rw [Fintype.card_prod, Fintype.card_fin, Fintype.card_coe] at hcard
    rw [hdeg] at hdim
    have : ((s.card * (n + 1) : ℕ) : ℤ) ≤ max (2 * ((n + M : ℕ) : ℤ) + 1) 0 :=
      (by exact_mod_cast hcard : ((s.card * (n + 1) : ℕ) : ℤ) ≤ _).trans hdim
    rw [max_eq_left (by positivity)] at this
    push_cast at this
    simp only [n] at this
    push_cast at this
    nlinarith
  have hrank : Module.rank F K ≤ (2 : ℕ) := rank_le key
  haveI : FiniteDimensional F K :=
    Module.rank_lt_aleph0_iff.mp (hrank.trans_lt (Cardinal.natCast_lt_aleph0))
  exact ⟨this, Module.finrank_le_of_rank_le hrank⟩

end ProperCurveFF

attribute [local instance] ProperCurveFF.finiteDimensional_lin

namespace CurveFFAut

variable (C : CurveFFAut k K Pt)

open ProperCurveFF CurveFFRR

/-- **The hyperelliptic-type involution in genus one.** For two distinct points `O ≠ O'` of a
curve of genus one there is an involution of the function field exchanging them: the
nontrivial automorphism of the quadratic extension `K / k(x)`, `x ∈ L(O + O')`. -/
private theorem exists_involution [CharZero k] (hg : C.genus = 1) {O O' : Pt} (hOO' : O ≠ O') :
    ∃ ρ : K ≃ₐ[k] K, ρ * ρ = 1 ∧ C.ptMap ρ O' = O := by
  classical
  have hg1 : 1 ≤ C.genus := by omega
  -- the function `x`
  set D2 : Pt →₀ ℤ := Finsupp.single O 1 + Finsupp.single O' 1
  have hrr := C.rr D2
  have hdeg2 : deg D2 = 2 := by simp only [D2, deg_add, deg_single]; norm_num
  rw [hdeg2, hg] at hrr
  obtain ⟨x, hxL, hxc⟩ := exists_mem_not_const (L := C.lin D2) (by push_cast at hrr; omega)
  have hx0 : x ≠ 0 := fun h => hxc 0 (by rw [h, map_zero])
  have hD2 : ∀ Q, D2 Q = (if O = Q then 1 else 0) + (if O' = Q then 1 else 0) := fun Q => by
    simp [D2, Finsupp.single_apply]
  rcases hxL with h | hxL
  · exact absurd h hx0
  have hxQ : ∀ Q, Q ≠ O → Q ≠ O' → 0 ≤ C.ord Q x := fun Q h1 h2 => by
    have := hxL Q; rw [hD2, if_neg (Ne.symm h1), if_neg (Ne.symm h2)] at this; omega
  have hxO : C.ord O x = -1 := by
    have h1 := hxL O; rw [hD2, if_pos rfl, if_neg hOO'.symm] at h1
    by_contra hne
    obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := C.const_of_mem_lin_single hg1 O' (f := x) (Or.inr fun Q => by
      rw [Finsupp.single_apply]
      by_cases hQ : O' = Q
      · subst hQ; rw [if_pos rfl]; have := hxL O'; rw [hD2, if_neg hOO', if_pos rfl] at this
        omega
      · rw [if_neg hQ]
        by_cases hQO : Q = O
        · subst hQO; omega
        · simpa using hxQ Q hQO (Ne.symm hQ))
    exact hxc c hc
  have hxO' : C.ord O' x = -1 := by
    have h1 := hxL O'; rw [hD2, if_neg hOO', if_pos rfl] at h1
    by_contra hne
    obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := C.const_of_mem_lin_single hg1 O (f := x) (Or.inr fun Q => by
      rw [Finsupp.single_apply]
      by_cases hQ : O = Q
      · subst hQ; rw [if_pos rfl]; omega
      · rw [if_neg hQ]
        by_cases hQO : Q = O'
        · subst hQO; omega
        · simpa using hxQ Q (Ne.symm hQ) hQO)
    exact hxc c hc
  -- the quadratic extension `K / k(x)`
  obtain ⟨hfd, hle⟩ := C.finrank_adjoin_le_two hOO' hxO hxO' hxQ
  set F := IntermediateField.adjoin k {x}
  haveI := hfd
  -- an element outside `k(x)`
  have hrr2 := C.rr ((2 : ℤ) • Finsupp.single O 1)
  rw [deg_smul, deg_single, hg] at hrr2
  obtain ⟨z, hzL, hzc⟩ := exists_mem_not_const (L := C.lin ((2 : ℤ) • Finsupp.single O 1))
    (by push_cast at hrr2; omega)
  have hz0 : z ≠ 0 := fun h => hzc 0 (by rw [h, map_zero])
  rcases hzL with h | hzL
  · exact absurd h hz0
  have hzQ : ∀ Q, Q ≠ O → 0 ≤ C.ord Q z := fun Q hQ => by
    simpa only [Finsupp.smul_apply, Finsupp.single_apply, if_neg (Ne.symm hQ), smul_zero,
      add_zero] using hzL Q
  have hzO : C.ord O z = -2 := by
    have h1 := hzL O
    simp only [Finsupp.smul_apply, Finsupp.single_eq_same, smul_eq_mul, mul_one] at h1
    have hneg : C.ord O z < 0 := by
      by_contra hnn
      obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := C.const z fun Q => by
        by_cases hQ : Q = O
        · subst hQ; omega
        · exact hzQ Q hQ
      exact hzc c hc
    by_contra hne
    obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := C.const_of_mem_lin_single hg1 O (f := z) (Or.inr fun Q => by
      rw [Finsupp.single_apply]
      by_cases hQ : O = Q
      · subst hQ; rw [if_pos rfl]; omega
      · rw [if_neg hQ]; simpa using hzQ Q (Ne.symm hQ))
    exact hzc c hc
  have hzF : z ∉ F := fun hz => by
    have := C.ord_eq_of_mem_adjoin hxO hxO' hz hz0
    have := hzQ O' (Ne.symm hOO')
    omega
  have hrank : finrank F K = 2 := by
    have h1 : finrank F K ≠ 1 := fun h1 => by
      obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := (finrank_eq_one_iff_of_nonzero' (1 : K) one_ne_zero).mp h1 z
      apply hzF
      rw [← hc, Algebra.smul_def, mul_one]
      exact c.2
    have h0 : 0 < finrank F K := Module.finrank_pos
    omega
  haveI : Algebra.IsQuadraticExtension F K := ⟨hrank⟩
  haveI : IsGalois F K := inferInstance
  have hcard : Nat.card Gal(K/F) = 2 := by rw [IsGalois.card_aut_eq_finrank, hrank]
  haveI : Nontrivial Gal(K/F) := Finite.one_lt_card_iff_nontrivial.mp (by omega)
  obtain ⟨ι, hι⟩ := exists_ne (1 : Gal(K/F))
  have hι2 : ι ^ 2 = 1 := by rw [← hcard]; exact pow_card_eq_one'
  set ρ : K ≃ₐ[k] K := ι.restrictScalars k
  have hρx : ρ x = x := ι.commutes ⟨x, IntermediateField.mem_adjoin_simple_self k x⟩
  have hρρ : ρ * ρ = 1 := by
    ext y
    change ι (ι y) = y
    simpa [pow_two] using congrArg (fun φ : Gal(K/F) => φ y) hι2
  have hρ1 : ρ ≠ 1 := fun h => hι (by
    ext y
    exact congrArg (fun φ : K ≃ₐ[k] K => φ y) h)
  refine ⟨ρ, hρρ, ?_⟩
  set π := C.ptMap ρ
  have hπ := C.isPointMap_ptMap ρ
  have hπx : ∀ Q, C.ord (π Q) x = C.ord Q x := fun Q => by rw [← hπ Q, hρx]
  have hpole : ∀ Q, C.ord Q x < 0 → Q = O ∨ Q = O' := fun Q hQ => by
    by_contra h; push Not at h; have := hxQ Q h.1 h.2; omega
  have hπO : π O = O' := by
    rcases hpole (π O) (by rw [hπx, hxO]; omega) with h | h
    · exfalso
      apply hρ1
      refine C.eq_one_of_fixes_uniformizer (π := π) hπ h (t := x⁻¹)
        (by rw [C.ord_inv O hx0, hxO]; rfl) (by rw [map_inv₀, hρx])
    · exact h
  rcases hpole (π O') (by rw [hπx, hxO']; omega) with h | h
  · exact h
  · exact absurd (C.ptMap_injective ρ (hπO.trans h.symm)) hOO'

omit [Field K] [Algebra k K] in
private theorem deg_cast_eq {Dv : Pt →₀ ℤ} {E : Pt →₀ ℤ} {B : Pt →₀ ℚ} {m : ℕ}
    (hDv : ∀ P, (Dv P : ℚ) = m * E P + m * B P) :
    (deg Dv : ℚ) = m * deg E + m * B.sum fun _ a => a := by
  classical
  have h1 : Dv.mapRange (Int.cast : ℤ → ℚ) Int.cast_zero =
      (m : ℚ) • E.mapRange (Int.cast : ℤ → ℚ) Int.cast_zero + (m : ℚ) • B := by
    ext P; simp [hDv P]
  have hsum : ∀ D : Pt →₀ ℤ, (deg D : ℚ) =
      (D.mapRange (Int.cast : ℤ → ℚ) Int.cast_zero).sum fun _ a => a := fun D => by
    rw [Finsupp.sum_mapRange_index (fun _ => rfl)]
    simp [deg, Finsupp.sum]
  rw [hsum Dv, h1, Finsupp.sum_add_index' (fun _ => rfl) (fun _ _ _ => rfl),
    Finsupp.sum_smul_index (fun _ => rfl), Finsupp.sum_smul_index (fun _ => rfl),
    ← Finsupp.mul_sum, ← Finsupp.mul_sum, ← hsum E]

/-- **Positive degree, genus at least one: finitely many automorphisms.** -/
private theorem finite_of_deg_pos [CharZero k] (hg : 1 ≤ C.genus) {B : Pt →₀ ℚ} {m : ℕ}
    {Dv : Pt →₀ ℤ} (hDv : ∀ P, (Dv P : ℚ) = m * C.canon P + m * B P) (hpos : 0 < deg Dv)
    (G : Set (K ≃ₐ[k] K)) (hG : ∀ σ ∈ G, ∀ P, B (C.ptMap σ P) = B P) : G.Finite := by
  set j : ℕ := 3 * C.genus + 2
  refine C.finite_of_twist hg (Dv := (j : ℤ) • Dv) ?_ G C.ptMap (fun σ => C.ptMap σ⁻¹)
    fun σ hσ => ⟨C.isPointMap_ptMap σ, C.isPointMap_ptMap σ⁻¹, C.mult σ ^ (j * m),
      pow_ne_zero _ (C.mult_ne_zero σ), fun P => ?_⟩
  · rw [deg_smul]
    have : (1 : ℤ) ≤ deg Dv := hpos
    simp only [j]; push_cast; nlinarith
  · rw [C.ord_pow P (C.mult_ne_zero σ), C.ord_mult]
    simp only [Finsupp.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul]
    have h1 := hDv P
    have h2 := hDv (C.ptMap σ P)
    rw [hG σ hσ P] at h2
    have : ((j * m : ℕ) : ℚ) * (C.canon (C.ptMap σ P) - C.canon P) + j * Dv P =
        j * Dv (C.ptMap σ P) := by
      rw [h1, h2]; push_cast; ring
    exact_mod_cast this

/-- **Genus zero, at least three marked points: finitely many automorphisms.** -/
private theorem finite_of_three_points (hg : C.genus = 0) {B : Pt →₀ ℚ} (h3 : 3 ≤ B.support.card)
    (G : Set (K ≃ₐ[k] K)) (hG : ∀ σ ∈ G, ∀ P, B (C.ptMap σ P) = B P) : G.Finite := by
  classical
  refine C.finite_of_mapsTo G C.ptMap (fun σ => C.ptMap σ⁻¹) (S := ↑B.support)
    (Finset.finite_toSet _) ?_ fun σ hσ => ⟨C.isPointMap_ptMap σ, C.isPointMap_ptMap σ⁻¹,
      fun P hP => ?_⟩
  · rw [Set.ncard_coe_finset, hg]; push_cast; omega
  · simp only [Finset.mem_coe, Finsupp.mem_support_iff] at hP ⊢
    rwa [hG σ hσ P]

private theorem finite_range_of_scalars {Dv : Pt →₀ ℤ} {m : ℕ} (G : Set (K ≃ₐ[k] K)) {S : Set k}
    (hS : S.Finite) (h : ∀ σ ∈ G, ∃ ε ∈ S, ∀ f ∈ C.lin Dv,
      σ f * C.mult σ ^ m = algebraMap k K ε * f) :
    (Set.range fun σ : G => fun f : C.lin Dv => (σ : K ≃ₐ[k] K) (f : K) * C.mult σ ^ m).Finite := by
  refine (hS.image fun ε => fun f : C.lin Dv => algebraMap k K ε * (f : K)).subset ?_
  rintro _ ⟨⟨σ, hσ⟩, rfl⟩
  obtain ⟨ε, hε, hεf⟩ := h σ hσ
  exact ⟨ε, hε, funext fun f => (hεf f f.2).symm⟩

/-- **Finite pluriform representations, abstractly.** Let `0 ≤ B ≤ 1` be a `ℚ`-divisor with
`deg (κ + B) ≥ 0`, and `D = m (κ + B)` integral. The automorphisms preserving `B` act on `L(D)`
by `f ↦ σ f · h_σ^m` through finitely many maps. -/
private theorem finite_range_twisted [CharZero k] {B : Pt →₀ ℚ} (hB : ∀ P, 0 ≤ B P ∧ B P ≤ 1)
    (hdeg : 0 ≤ (deg C.canon : ℚ) + B.sum fun _ a => a) {m : ℕ} (hm : 0 < m)
    {Dv : Pt →₀ ℤ} (hDv : ∀ P, (Dv P : ℚ) = m * C.canon P + m * B P) (G : Set (K ≃ₐ[k] K))
    (hG : ∀ σ ∈ G, ∀ P, B (C.ptMap σ P) = B P) :
    (Set.range fun σ : G => fun f : C.lin Dv => (σ : K ≃ₐ[k] K) (f : K) * C.mult σ ^ m).Finite := by
  classical
  have hfinG : G.Finite → (Set.range fun σ : G => fun f : C.lin Dv =>
      (σ : K ≃ₐ[k] K) (f : K) * C.mult σ ^ m).Finite := fun h => by
    haveI := h.to_subtype; exact Set.finite_range _
  set Sm := B.sum fun _ a => a
  have hSm : Sm = ∑ P ∈ B.support, B P := rfl
  have hS0 : 0 ≤ Sm := Finset.sum_nonneg fun P _ => (hB P).1
  have hSle : Sm ≤ B.support.card := by
    rw [hSm, Finset.card_eq_sum_ones, Nat.cast_sum]
    exact Finset.sum_le_sum fun P _ => by simpa using (hB P).2
  have hcanon : (deg C.canon : ℚ) = 2 * C.genus - 2 := by exact_mod_cast C.deg_canon
  have hdegDv := deg_cast_eq hDv
  rcases hdeg.lt_or_eq with hpos | hzero
  · apply hfinG
    by_cases hg : 1 ≤ C.genus
    · refine C.finite_of_deg_pos hg hDv ?_ G hG
      have : (0 : ℚ) < deg Dv := by
        rw [hdegDv]
        have : (0 : ℚ) < m := by exact_mod_cast hm
        nlinarith
      exact_mod_cast this
    · have hg0 : C.genus = 0 := by omega
      refine C.finite_of_three_points hg0 ?_ G hG
      rw [hcanon, hg0] at hpos
      have : (2 : ℚ) < B.support.card := by push_cast at hpos; linarith
      exact_mod_cast this
  · rcases Nat.lt_or_ge C.genus 2 with hg | hg
    · interval_cases hgv : C.genus
      · -- genus zero, degree two
        by_cases h3 : 3 ≤ B.support.card
        · exact hfinG (C.finite_of_three_points hgv h3 G hG)
        have hS2 : Sm = 2 := by rw [hcanon] at hzero; push_cast at hzero; linarith
        have hcard : B.support.card = 2 := by
          have : (2 : ℚ) ≤ B.support.card := hS2 ▸ hSle
          have : 2 ≤ B.support.card := by exact_mod_cast this
          omega
        obtain ⟨P₁, P₂, h12, hsupp⟩ := Finset.card_eq_two.mp hcard
        have hsum2 : B P₁ + B P₂ = 2 := by
          rw [← hS2, hSm, hsupp, Finset.sum_pair h12]
        have hB1 : B P₁ = 1 := by linarith [(hB P₁).2, (hB P₂).2]
        have hB2 : B P₂ = 1 := by linarith [(hB P₁).2, (hB P₂).2]
        have hBQ : ∀ Q, Q ≠ P₁ → Q ≠ P₂ → B Q = 0 := fun Q h1 h2 => by
          have : Q ∉ B.support := by rw [hsupp]; simp [h1, h2]
          exact Finsupp.notMem_support_iff.mp this
        have hBiff : ∀ Q, B Q ≠ 0 ↔ (Q = P₁ ∨ Q = P₂) := fun Q => by
          constructor
          · intro h; by_contra h'; push Not at h'; exact h (hBQ Q h'.1 h'.2)
          · rintro (rfl | rfl) <;> simp [hB1, hB2]
        have hDv' : Dv = (m : ℤ) • C.canon +
            (m : ℤ) • (Finsupp.single P₁ 1 + Finsupp.single P₂ 1) := by
          ext Q
          simp only [Finsupp.add_apply, Finsupp.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul]
          have hval : (((Finsupp.single P₁ (1 : ℤ)) Q : ℤ) : ℚ) +
              (((Finsupp.single P₂ (1 : ℤ)) Q : ℤ) : ℚ) = B Q := by
            simp only [Finsupp.single_apply]
            by_cases h1 : Q = P₁
            · subst h1; simp [h12, Ne.symm h12, hB1]
            · by_cases h2 : Q = P₂
              · subst h2; simp [h1, Ne.symm h1, hB2]
              · simp [h1, h2, Ne.symm h1, Ne.symm h2, hBQ Q h1 h2]
          apply Int.cast_injective (α := ℚ)
          push_cast
          rw [hDv Q, ← hval]
        subst hDv'
        refine C.finite_range_of_scalars G (S := {1, (-1) ^ m}) (Set.toFinite _) fun σ hσ => ?_
        obtain ⟨ε, hε, hεf⟩ := C.twoPoint_action hgv h12 m σ fun Q => by
          rw [← hBiff, ← hBiff, hG σ hσ Q]
        exact ⟨ε, by rcases hε with rfl | rfl <;> simp, hεf⟩
      · -- genus one, no boundary
        have hS0' : Sm = 0 := by rw [hcanon] at hzero; push_cast at hzero; linarith
        have hB0 : ∀ P, B P = 0 := fun P => by
          by_cases hP : P ∈ B.support
          · exact (Finset.sum_eq_zero_iff_of_nonneg (fun P _ => (hB P).1)).mp hS0' P hP
          · exact Finsupp.notMem_support_iff.mp hP
        have hDv' : Dv = (m : ℤ) • C.canon := by
          ext P; have h := hDv P; rw [hB0 P, mul_zero, add_zero] at h
          simp only [Finsupp.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul]; exact_mod_cast h
        subst hDv'
        obtain ⟨S, hS, hSσ⟩ := C.genusOne_finite_scalars hgv m fun O O' h =>
          C.exists_involution hgv h
        exact C.finite_range_of_scalars G hS fun σ _ => hSσ σ
    · exfalso
      rw [hcanon] at hzero
      have : (2 : ℚ) ≤ C.genus := by exact_mod_cast hg
      linarith

end CurveFFAut

